window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-28-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-28-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 28 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000071981","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If 213 &#8594; 040109, 738 &#8594; 490964, then 912 &#8594; ? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 213 &#8594; 040109, 738 &#8594; 490964, तो 912 &#8594; ? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"729145"},"2":{"en":"225491"},"3":{"en":"810104"},"4":{"en":"496401"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Each digit of the number is written as its own square in two places: 2² = 04, 1² = 01 and 3² = 09, which gives 040109 ✔<br>For 738 the same gives 49, 09 and 64, that is 490964 ✔<br>For 912: 9² = 81, 1² = 01 and 2² = 04, so the code is 810104<br>Hence the missing code is 810104<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 810104.</b>","hi":"संख्या के प्रत्येक अंक को उसके वर्ग के रूप में दो स्थानों में लिखा जाता है: 2² = 04, 1² = 01 तथा 3² = 09, जिससे 040109 मिलता है ✔<br>738 के लिए इसी प्रकार 49, 09 तथा 64 अर्थात् 490964 मिलता है ✔<br>912 के लिए: 9² = 81, 1² = 01 तथा 2² = 04, अतः कूट 810104 है<br>इसलिए लुप्त कूट 810104 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 810104 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000071982","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"If x + y = 10 and xy = 21, find x² + y². [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि x + y = 10 तथा xy = 21 है, तो x² + y² ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"100"},"2":{"en":"58"},"3":{"en":"64"},"4":{"en":"79"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"We know that (x + y)² = x² + y² + 2xy<br>So 10² = x² + y² + 2 × 21, that is 100 = x² + y² + 42<br>Hence x² + y² = 100 − 42 = 58<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 58.</b>","hi":"हम जानते हैं कि (x + y)² = x² + y² + 2xy<br>अतः 10² = x² + y² + 2 × 21, अर्थात् 100 = x² + y² + 42<br>इसलिए x² + y² = 100 − 42 = 58<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 58 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000071983","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"In a class, 20 students like Reading, 15 like Drawing, and 10 like both. How many like only Reading? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक कक्षा में 20 विद्यार्थी पढ़ना पसंद करते हैं, 15 चित्रकारी पसंद करते हैं तथा 10 दोनों पसंद करते हैं। कितने विद्यार्थी केवल पढ़ना पसंद करते हैं? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The students who like only Reading are those who like Reading but not Drawing<br>That number is 20 − 10 = 10<br>So 10 students like only Reading<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 10.</b>","hi":"केवल पढ़ना पसंद करने वाले वे विद्यार्थी हैं जो पढ़ना पसंद करते हैं परंतु चित्रकारी नहीं<br>यह संख्या 20 − 10 = 10 है<br>अतः 10 विद्यार्थी केवल पढ़ना पसंद करते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000071984","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the next number in the series?<br>2, 12, 30, 56, 90, ? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"श्रेणी में अगली संख्या क्या है?<br>2, 12, 30, 56, 90, ? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"128"},"2":{"en":"132"},"3":{"en":"140"},"4":{"en":"150"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The terms are the products of consecutive pairs of numbers: 1 × 2 = 2, 3 × 4 = 12, 5 × 6 = 30, 7 × 8 = 56 and 9 × 10 = 90<br>The next pair is 11 × 12 = 132<br>So the next number is 132<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 132.</b>","hi":"पद क्रमागत संख्या-युग्मों के गुणनफल हैं: 1 × 2 = 2, 3 × 4 = 12, 5 × 6 = 30, 7 × 8 = 56 तथा 9 × 10 = 90<br>अगला युग्म 11 × 12 = 132 है<br>अतः अगली संख्या 132 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 132 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000071985","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"ORGANIC\" is written as \"PULBQND.\" How will \"MACHINE\" be written? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"ORGANIC\" को \"PULBQND\" लिखा जाता है। \"MACHINE\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"NDIHLSF"},"2":{"en":"NDHLISF"},"3":{"en":"NDIIHLSE"},"4":{"en":"NDHILSF"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In ORGANIC the letters move by +1, +3, +5 and then again +1, +3, +5: O→P, R→U, G→L, A→B, N→Q, I→N and C→D<br>Applying the same steps to MACHINE: M→N, A→D, C→H, H→I, I→L, N→S and E→F<br>So MACHINE is written as NDHILSF<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): NDHILSF.</b>","hi":"ORGANIC में अक्षर +1, +3, +5 तथा फिर +1, +3, +5 से बढ़ते हैं: O→P, R→U, G→L, A→B, N→Q, I→N तथा C→D<br>MACHINE पर वही चरण लगाने से M→N, A→D, C→H, H→I, I→L, N→S तथा E→F<br>अतः MACHINE को NDHILSF लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): NDHILSF है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000071986","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In this following question, four words have been given, out of which three are alike in some manner and the fourth one is different. Choose odd one out. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में चार शब्द दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी प्रकार समान हैं और चौथा भिन्न है। विषम शब्द चुनिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Microscope","hi":"सूक्ष्मदर्शी"},"2":{"en":"Centrifuge","hi":"सेंट्रीफ्यूज"},"3":{"en":"Magnifying Glass","hi":"आवर्धक लेंस"},"4":{"en":"Telescope","hi":"दूरबीन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A microscope, a magnifying glass and a telescope are all optical instruments used to see things larger or farther<br>A centrifuge is not an optical instrument; it spins samples to separate their parts<br>So Centrifuge is the odd one out<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Centrifuge.</b>","hi":"सूक्ष्मदर्शी, आवर्धक लेंस तथा दूरबीन सभी प्रकाशिक यंत्र हैं जिनसे वस्तुएँ बड़ी या दूर से देखी जाती हैं<br>सेंट्रीफ्यूज प्रकाशिक यंत्र नहीं है; यह नमूनों को घुमाकर उनके भाग अलग करता है<br>अतः सेंट्रीफ्यूज विषम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): सेंट्रीफ्यूज है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000071987","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Ananya is the daughter-in-law of Bharat. Bharat's wife is Chitra. Chitra's only son is Dev. Dev has no other siblings except his sister Ekta.<br>How many children does Chitra have? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अनन्या, भरत की पुत्रवधू है। भरत की पत्नी चित्रा है। चित्रा का एकमात्र पुत्र देव है। देव की अपनी बहन एकता के अतिरिक्त कोई अन्य सहोदर नहीं है।<br>चित्रा के कितने बच्चे हैं? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"Cannot be determined","hi":"निर्धारित नहीं किया जा सकता"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Chitra's only son is Dev, so Dev is her one child<br>Dev has no siblings except his sister Ekta, so Ekta is the daughter of Chitra and is her second child<br>Chitra therefore has two children, Dev and Ekta, and Ananya being her daughter-in-law only confirms the marriage of Dev<br><svg width=\"184\" height=\"196\" viewBox=\"0 0 184 196\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M34 19H118M34 25H118\"/><path d=\"M34 85H22M34 91H22\"/><path d=\"M76 28V55H28V78\"/><path d=\"M76 28V55H124V78\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Bharat+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Bharat+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Chitra−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Chitra−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Dev+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Dev+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Ekta−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Ekta−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Ananya−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Ananya−</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2.</b>","hi":"चित्रा का एकमात्र पुत्र देव है, अतः देव उसका एक बच्चा है<br>देव की अपनी बहन एकता के अतिरिक्त कोई सहोदर नहीं है, अतः एकता चित्रा की पुत्री और उसका दूसरा बच्चा है<br>इसलिए चित्रा के दो बच्चे हैं, देव तथा एकता, और अनन्या के पुत्रवधू होने से केवल देव का विवाह पुष्ट होता है<br><svg width=\"184\" height=\"196\" viewBox=\"0 0 184 196\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M34 19H118M34 25H118\"/><path d=\"M34 85H22M34 91H22\"/><path d=\"M76 28V55H28V78\"/><path d=\"M76 28V55H124V78\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Bharat+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Bharat+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Chitra−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Chitra−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Dev+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Dev+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Ekta−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Ekta−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Ananya−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Ananya−</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000071988","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">91</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">33</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">91</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">33</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40"},"2":{"en":"44"},"3":{"en":"64"},"4":{"en":"50"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In every row the third number is the first number multiplied by one less than the second number: 7 × 13 = 91 ✔ and 3 × 11 = 33 ✔<br>In the third row the same rule gives 10 × 5 = 50<br>So the missing number is 50<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 50.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में तीसरी संख्या पहली संख्या को दूसरी संख्या से एक कम के गुणनफल के बराबर है: 7 × 13 = 91 ✔ तथा 3 × 11 = 33 ✔<br>तीसरी पंक्ति में वही नियम 10 × 5 = 50 देता है<br>अतः लुप्त संख्या 50 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 50 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000071989","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern in fig. (X) by selecting one of the figures from the four alternatives :<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e86cd-14f0-7251-a194-042bd02150fe_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005059794\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1] [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आकृति (X) का पैटर्न पूरा करने के लिए चार विकल्पों में से एक आकृति चुनिए:<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019e86cd-14f0-7251-a194-042bd02150fe_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147415962\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1] [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8bff-afbb-7e28-a8ac-38a6e4b11cd3_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005085139\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ebad5-3759-7e10-916e-e2934a355241_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147436004\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8bff-afbb-7e28-a8ac-38a782ef52eb_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005102062\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ebad5-3759-7e10-916e-e294a92eb9d6_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147456047\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8bff-afbb-7e28-a8ac-38a82dc5f974_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005137088\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ebad5-3759-7e10-916e-e29513abb85b_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147476088\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8bff-afbb-7e28-a8ac-38a90b79eb94_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005164781\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ebad5-3759-7e10-916e-e296fe7cb289_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147496130\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is a rectangle carrying a large ellipse, two concentric circles at the centre, both diagonals and the vertical and horizontal centre lines, with a dark dot exactly at the centre<br>The missing part is the lower right quarter, so it must carry the arcs of the ellipse and the inner circle coming down from the top left corner together with the half diagonal running to the bottom right corner<br>Option A shows exactly these curved arcs meeting the diagonal at the corner of the part, while the other options shift the curves or add straight lines that are not in the original<br>Hence the figure of option 1 completes the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8bff-afbb-7e28-a8ac-38a6e4b11cd3_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005085139\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) एक आयत है जिसमें बड़ा दीर्घवृत्त, केंद्र पर दो संकेंद्री वृत्त, दोनों विकर्ण तथा ऊर्ध्व और क्षैतिज मध्य रेखाएँ हैं, और काला बिंदु ठीक केंद्र पर है<br>लुप्त भाग निचला दायाँ चतुर्थांश है, अतः उसमें ऊपर बाएँ कोने से नीचे आती दीर्घवृत्त तथा भीतरी वृत्त की चापें और निचले दाएँ कोने तक जाता आधा विकर्ण होना चाहिए<br>विकल्प A में यही वक्र चापें भाग के कोने पर विकर्ण से मिलती हैं, जबकि अन्य विकल्प वक्रों को खिसका देते हैं या मूल में न होने वाली सीधी रेखाएँ जोड़ देते हैं<br>अतः विकल्प 1 की आकृति पैटर्न पूरा करती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ebad5-3759-7e10-916e-e2934a355241_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147436004\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e86cd-14f0-7251-a194-042bd02150fe_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005059794","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019e86cd-14f0-7251-a194-042bd02150fe_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147415962"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8bff-afbb-7e28-a8ac-38a6e4b11cd3_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005085139","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ebad5-3759-7e10-916e-e2934a355241_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147436004"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8bff-afbb-7e28-a8ac-38a782ef52eb_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005102062","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ebad5-3759-7e10-916e-e294a92eb9d6_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147456047"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8bff-afbb-7e28-a8ac-38a82dc5f974_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005137088","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ebad5-3759-7e10-916e-e29513abb85b_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147476088"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8bff-afbb-7e28-a8ac-38a90b79eb94_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005164781","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ebad5-3759-7e10-916e-e296fe7cb289_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147496130"]},"solution":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8bff-afbb-7e28-a8ac-38a6e4b11cd3_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005085139","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ebad5-3759-7e10-916e-e2934a355241_HI.jpg?edu=639294382147436004"]}},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000071990","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the odd number pair from the given alternatives. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से विषम संख्या-युग्म चुनिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"31, 961"},"2":{"en":"28, 784"},"3":{"en":"27, 720"},"4":{"en":"24, 576"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In the first, second and fourth pairs the second number is the square of the first: 31² = 961 ✔, 28² = 784 ✔ and 24² = 576 ✔<br>For the third pair 27² = 729, not 720 ✘<br>So 27, 720 is the odd pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 27, 720.</b>","hi":"पहले, दूसरे तथा चौथे युग्म में दूसरी संख्या पहली संख्या का वर्ग है: 31² = 961 ✔, 28² = 784 ✔ तथा 24² = 576 ✔<br>तीसरे युग्म के लिए 27² = 729 है, 720 नहीं ✘<br>अतः 27, 720 विषम युग्म है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 27, 720 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000071991","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which centre code does not follow the pattern: \"Letter, Digit, Letter, Digit\" in alternating order? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा केंद्र कूट \"अक्षर, अंक, अक्षर, अंक\" के बारी-बारी क्रम का पालन नहीं करता? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A1B2"},"2":{"en":"X5Y9"},"3":{"en":"M2N4"},"4":{"en":"3K4L"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The pattern needs a letter, then a digit, then a letter and then a digit<br>A1B2, X5Y9 and M2N4 all begin with a letter and keep the letter-digit order<br>3K4L begins with a digit and ends with a letter, so the alternating order is broken<br>Hence 3K4L does not follow the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 3K4L.</b>","hi":"पैटर्न में पहले अक्षर, फिर अंक, फिर अक्षर तथा फिर अंक चाहिए<br>A1B2, X5Y9 तथा M2N4 सभी अक्षर से शुरू होकर अक्षर-अंक क्रम रखते हैं<br>3K4L अंक से शुरू होकर अक्षर पर समाप्त होता है, अतः बारी-बारी क्रम टूट जाता है<br>इसलिए 3K4L पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 3K4L है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000071992","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>ANK, CMM, ELO, ? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न जाँचिए और श्रेणी में अगला अक्षर-समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>ANK, CMM, ELO, ? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"GIQ"},"2":{"en":"GKQ"},"3":{"en":"GKP"},"4":{"en":"GKR"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The first letters A, C, E move two places ahead each time, so the next first letter is G<br>The second letters N, M, L move one place back each time, so the next second letter is K<br>The third letters K, M, O move two places ahead each time, so the next third letter is Q<br>Hence the next set of letters is GKQ<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): GKQ.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर A, C, E प्रत्येक बार दो स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला पहला अक्षर G है<br>दूसरे अक्षर N, M, L प्रत्येक बार एक स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः अगला दूसरा अक्षर K है<br>तीसरे अक्षर K, M, O प्रत्येक बार दो स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला तीसरा अक्षर Q है<br>इसलिए अगला अक्षर-समूह GKQ है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): GKQ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000071993","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"From the word 'TRANSPIRATIONAL', identify which of the given options can be formed. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शब्द 'TRANSPIRATIONAL' से पहचानिए कि दिए गए विकल्पों में से कौन-सा बनाया जा सकता है। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Aspirant"},"2":{"en":"Transparent"},"3":{"en":"Respiration"},"4":{"en":"Spiritual"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"TRANSPIRATIONAL has the letters T, R, A, N, S, P, I, R, A, T, I, O, N, A, L, so it has three A's, two each of R, T, N and I, and one each of S, P, O and L<br>ASPIRANT needs A, S, P, I, R, A, N, T, and every one of these letters is available in the required number<br>TRANSPARENT needs an E, RESPIRATION needs an E and SPIRITUAL needs a U, and none of these letters is present in the word<br>So only Aspirant can be formed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Aspirant.</b>","hi":"TRANSPIRATIONAL में अक्षर T, R, A, N, S, P, I, R, A, T, I, O, N, A, L हैं, अतः इसमें तीन A, दो-दो R, T, N तथा I तथा एक-एक S, P, O और L है<br>ASPIRANT के लिए A, S, P, I, R, A, N, T चाहिए और ये सभी अक्षर आवश्यक संख्या में उपलब्ध हैं<br>TRANSPARENT में E, RESPIRATION में E तथा SPIRITUAL में U चाहिए, और इनमें से कोई अक्षर शब्द में नहीं है<br>अतः केवल Aspirant बनाया जा सकता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): Aspirant है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000071994","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"Which Venn diagram correctly shows the relationship among Electronics, laptop, and oven?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e8f-c6d5-76d3-9feb-a1cdaa159f52_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005953988\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1] [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा वेन आरेख Electronics, laptop तथा oven के बीच संबंध सही दर्शाता है?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019e8e8f-c6d5-76d3-9feb-a1cdaa159f52_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148111068\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1] [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e93-e45a-7789-befc-88f3c406b9a3_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005994055\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f2729-2b96-7e92-accd-2923181e2b55_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148139207\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e93-e45a-7789-befc-88f40a60ba0e_EN.jpg?edu=639294382006034120\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f2729-2b96-7e92-accd-29243a785afe_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148164253\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e93-e45a-7789-befc-88f545a144cb_EN.jpg?edu=639294382006076324\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f2729-2b96-7e92-accd-292532fa2254_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148201313\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e93-e45a-7789-befc-88f6f3eca5c8_EN.jpg?edu=639294382006120265\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f2729-2b96-7e92-accd-2926e9bab7ee_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148229212\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Laptops and ovens are both electronic appliances, so both of their circles lie inside the big circle of electronics<br>No laptop is an oven, so the two small circles do not overlap each other<br>Only the first diagram shows two separate circles inside one large circle<br>Hence the first diagram is correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e93-e45a-7789-befc-88f3c406b9a3_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005994055\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"लैपटॉप और ओवन दोनों इलेक्ट्रॉनिक उपकरण हैं, अतः दोनों के वृत्त इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स के बड़े वृत्त के भीतर हैं<br>कोई लैपटॉप ओवन नहीं है, अतः दोनों छोटे वृत्त एक-दूसरे को नहीं काटते<br>केवल पहला आरेख एक बड़े वृत्त के भीतर दो अलग वृत्त दर्शाता है<br>अतः पहला आरेख सही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f2729-2b96-7e92-accd-2923181e2b55_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148139207\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e8f-c6d5-76d3-9feb-a1cdaa159f52_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005953988","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019e8e8f-c6d5-76d3-9feb-a1cdaa159f52_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148111068"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e93-e45a-7789-befc-88f3c406b9a3_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005994055","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f2729-2b96-7e92-accd-2923181e2b55_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148139207"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e93-e45a-7789-befc-88f40a60ba0e_EN.jpg?edu=639294382006034120","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f2729-2b96-7e92-accd-29243a785afe_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148164253"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e93-e45a-7789-befc-88f545a144cb_EN.jpg?edu=639294382006076324","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f2729-2b96-7e92-accd-292532fa2254_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148201313"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e93-e45a-7789-befc-88f6f3eca5c8_EN.jpg?edu=639294382006120265","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f2729-2b96-7e92-accd-2926e9bab7ee_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148229212"]},"solution":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e8e93-e45a-7789-befc-88f3c406b9a3_EN.jpg?edu=639294382005994055","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f2729-2b96-7e92-accd-2923181e2b55_HI.jpg?edu=639294382148139207"]}},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000071995","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If we interchange signs + and ×, and numbers 5 and 3, which of the given equations in the options is satisfied? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि हम + तथा × चिह्नों को और संख्याओं 5 तथा 3 को परस्पर बदल दें, तो विकल्पों में दिया कौन-सा समीकरण संतुष्ट होता है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 × 3 + 2 = 18"},"2":{"en":"3 × 5 + 4 = 19"},"3":{"en":"5 + 3 × 6 = 21"},"4":{"en":"2 + 5 × 3 = 13"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Interchanging + with × and 5 with 3 turns the third equation into 3 × 5 + 6 = 15 + 6 = 21 ✔<br>The first becomes 3 × 5 + 2 = 17, the second 5 + 3 × 4 = 17 and the fourth 2 × 3 + 5 = 11, so none of them is satisfied<br>Hence the third equation is the correct one<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 5 + 3 × 6 = 21.</b>","hi":"+ के स्थान पर × तथा 5 के स्थान पर 3 रखने से तीसरा समीकरण 3 × 5 + 6 = 15 + 6 = 21 बनता है ✔<br>पहला 3 × 5 + 2 = 17, दूसरा 5 + 3 × 4 = 17 तथा चौथा 2 × 3 + 5 = 11 बनता है, अतः कोई भी संतुष्ट नहीं होता<br>इसलिए तीसरा समीकरण सही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 5 + 3 × 6 = 21 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000071996","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The computer is considered one of the most significant inventions made by humankind.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. No other invention can be considered superior to the computer.<br>II. Computers have contributed to the progress and benefit of humanity. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कंप्यूटर को मानव जाति के सबसे महत्वपूर्ण आविष्कारों में से एक माना जाता है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कंप्यूटर से श्रेष्ठ कोई अन्य आविष्कार नहीं माना जा सकता।<br>II. कंप्यूटर ने मानवता की प्रगति तथा लाभ में योगदान दिया है। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Calling the computer one of the most significant inventions says that it stands among the greatest, not that it is greater than all others, so conclusion I does not follow<br>An invention counted as most significant is significant because it helped human progress, so conclusion II follows<br>Hence only conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only Conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"कंप्यूटर को सबसे महत्वपूर्ण आविष्कारों में से एक कहना यह बताता है कि वह महान आविष्कारों में है, यह नहीं कि वह सबसे श्रेष्ठ है, अतः निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता<br>सबसे महत्वपूर्ण गिना गया आविष्कार इसलिए महत्वपूर्ण है कि उसने मानव प्रगति में सहायता की, अतः निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000071997","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Authorities have increased penalties for traffic violations and installed additional speed-monitoring cameras on highways.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. Traffic violations will completely stop in the future.<br>II. The authorities believe stricter enforcement can improve road safety.<br>III. Road safety is a concern for the authorities. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>अधिकारियों ने यातायात उल्लंघनों के लिए दंड बढ़ा दिए हैं तथा राजमार्गों पर अतिरिक्त गति-निगरानी कैमरे लगाए हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. भविष्य में यातायात उल्लंघन पूरी तरह बंद हो जाएँगे।<br>II. अधिकारियों का मानना है कि कड़ा प्रवर्तन सड़क सुरक्षा सुधार सकता है।<br>III. सड़क सुरक्षा अधिकारियों के लिए चिंता का विषय है। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only inferences I and II follow.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I और II निकलते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"All inferences follow.","hi":"सभी निष्कर्ष निकलते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Only inferences I and III follow.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I और III निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Only inferences II and III follow.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II और III निकलते हैं।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Higher penalties and more cameras are enforcement steps taken in the belief that they will improve safety, so II follows<br>Spending on these measures shows that road safety matters to the authorities, so III follows<br>No measure can promise that every violation will end, so the word completely makes I too strong and it does not follow<br>Hence only inferences II and III follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only inferences II and III follow..</b>","hi":"दंड बढ़ाना तथा अधिक कैमरे लगाना ऐसे प्रवर्तन कदम हैं जो इस विश्वास से लिए जाते हैं कि उनसे सुरक्षा सुधरेगी, अतः II निकलता है<br>इन उपायों पर व्यय यह दर्शाता है कि सड़क सुरक्षा अधिकारियों के लिए महत्वपूर्ण है, अतः III निकलता है<br>कोई उपाय यह वचन नहीं दे सकता कि हर उल्लंघन समाप्त हो जाएगा, अतः 'पूरी तरह' शब्द I को अत्यधिक दृढ़ बना देता है और वह नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II और III निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल निष्कर्ष II और III निकलते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000071998","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A survey found that households using LED bulbs consumed less electricity on average than households using conventional bulbs.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The use of LED bulbs ensures identical electricity consumption in all households.<br>II. The use of LED bulbs may help households reduce electricity consumption. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक सर्वेक्षण में पाया गया कि एलईडी बल्ब प्रयोग करने वाले परिवारों ने पारंपरिक बल्ब प्रयोग करने वाले परिवारों की तुलना में औसतन कम बिजली खपत की।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. एलईडी बल्बों का प्रयोग सभी परिवारों में समान बिजली खपत सुनिश्चित करता है।<br>II. एलईडी बल्बों का प्रयोग परिवारों को बिजली खपत घटाने में सहायता कर सकता है। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The survey compares averages and shows that LED users used less electricity, which suggests that LEDs can help reduce consumption, so conclusion II follows<br>Averages never make every household identical, so conclusion I does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"सर्वेक्षण औसत की तुलना करता है और दर्शाता है कि एलईडी प्रयोग करने वालों ने कम बिजली खपत की, जिससे संकेत मिलता है कि एलईडी खपत घटाने में सहायक हो सकते हैं, अतः निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br>औसत कभी सभी परिवारों को समान नहीं बनाता, अतः निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000071999","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a specific casing code, every alternate letter starting from E is written in lowercase. Letters A, B, C, and D are written in uppercase, while from E onwards, the alphabet alternates between lowercase and uppercase (i.e., A, B, C, D, e, F, g, H...). Under this rule, how will the word 'NOVEMBER' be written? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक विशिष्ट केसिंग कूट में E से शुरू होकर प्रत्येक एकांतर अक्षर छोटे अक्षरों में लिखा जाता है। अक्षर A, B, C तथा D बड़े अक्षरों में लिखे जाते हैं, जबकि E से आगे वर्णमाला छोटे और बड़े अक्षरों के बीच बदलती है (अर्थात् A, B, C, D, e, F, g, H...)। इस नियम के अनुसार शब्द 'NOVEMBER' कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"NoVemBeR"},"2":{"en":"NOvEmBeR"},"3":{"en":"NoveMBer"},"4":{"en":"NOvEmBer"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the rule the odd-numbered letters from E onwards are small and the even-numbered ones are capital: E(5) small, F(6) capital, G(7) small, H(8) capital and so on<br>So the letters with odd positions are small and the letters with even positions are capital, and A to D are always capital<br>For NOVEMBER: N(14) capital, O(15) small, V(22) capital, E(5) small, M(13) small, B(2) capital, E(5) small and R(18) capital<br>Hence NOVEMBER is written as NoVemBeR<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): NoVemBeR.</b>","hi":"नियम में E से आगे विषम स्थान वाले अक्षर छोटे तथा सम स्थान वाले बड़े होते हैं: E(5) छोटा, F(6) बड़ा, G(7) छोटा, H(8) बड़ा इत्यादि<br>अतः विषम स्थान वाले अक्षर छोटे तथा सम स्थान वाले बड़े लिखे जाते हैं, और A से D तक सदैव बड़े रहते हैं<br>NOVEMBER के लिए: N(14) बड़ा, O(15) छोटा, V(22) बड़ा, E(5) छोटा, M(13) छोटा, B(2) बड़ा, E(5) छोटा तथा R(18) बड़ा<br>इसलिए NOVEMBER को NoVemBeR लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): NoVemBeR है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000072000","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Select the correct mirror image of the given combination when the mirror at right side of the image.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed41b-db28-7fb4-847e-09761e0094bc_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007505381\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1] [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए संयोजन का सही दर्पण प्रतिबिंब चुनिए जब दर्पण आकृति के दाईं ओर है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ed41b-db28-7fb4-847e-09761e0094bc_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149334850\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1] [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed420-4350-79f0-bdb9-98f89f211d3a_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007565549\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f4a86-5f24-7426-93ac-44542e3834c5_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149371818\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed420-4350-79f0-bdb9-98f95ad88f22_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007623468\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f4a86-5f24-7426-93ac-4455312237f0_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149419965\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed420-4350-79f0-bdb9-98faa6dc79f0_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007680978\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f4a86-5f24-7426-93ac-4456764b245c_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149463067\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed420-4350-79f0-bdb9-98fbddb97583_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007741513\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f4a86-5f24-7426-93ac-445787d31874_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149509590\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"With the mirror on the right, the combination b 4 d 5 t is reversed in order and each character is flipped horizontally while keeping its height<br>So the image must read from the flipped t, then 5, then d, then 4 and finally the flipped b<br>Only the first option keeps this exact order with every character properly flipped, while the others change the order of the middle characters<br>Hence the first option is the correct mirror image<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed420-4350-79f0-bdb9-98f89f211d3a_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007565549\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"दर्पण दाईं ओर होने पर संयोजन b 4 d 5 t का क्रम उलट जाता है और प्रत्येक अक्षर ऊँचाई वही रखते हुए क्षैतिज रूप से पलटता है<br>अतः प्रतिबिंब पलटे हुए t से शुरू होकर 5, फिर d, फिर 4 तथा अंत में पलटे हुए b तक पढ़ा जाना चाहिए<br>केवल पहले विकल्प में यही क्रम है और प्रत्येक अक्षर ठीक से पलटा है, जबकि अन्य विकल्प बीच के अक्षरों का क्रम बदल देते हैं<br>अतः पहला विकल्प सही दर्पण प्रतिबिंब है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f4a86-5f24-7426-93ac-44542e3834c5_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149371818\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed41b-db28-7fb4-847e-09761e0094bc_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007505381","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019ed41b-db28-7fb4-847e-09761e0094bc_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149334850"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed420-4350-79f0-bdb9-98f89f211d3a_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007565549","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f4a86-5f24-7426-93ac-44542e3834c5_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149371818"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed420-4350-79f0-bdb9-98f95ad88f22_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007623468","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f4a86-5f24-7426-93ac-4455312237f0_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149419965"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed420-4350-79f0-bdb9-98faa6dc79f0_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007680978","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f4a86-5f24-7426-93ac-4456764b245c_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149463067"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed420-4350-79f0-bdb9-98fbddb97583_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007741513","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f4a86-5f24-7426-93ac-445787d31874_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149509590"]},"solution":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019ed420-4350-79f0-bdb9-98f89f211d3a_EN.jpg?edu=639294382007565549","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f4a86-5f24-7426-93ac-44542e3834c5_HI.jpg?edu=639294382149371818"]}},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000072001","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Dildar is preparing a policy report that will be submitted to a review committee the following morning. The report's conclusions may influence important administrative decisions, making accuracy, credibility, and verifiability of information essential. With limited time available, Dildar must select the most reliable source of data.<br>Which source should Dildar rely upon? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिलदार एक नीति रिपोर्ट तैयार कर रहा है जो अगली सुबह समीक्षा समिति को प्रस्तुत की जाएगी। रिपोर्ट के निष्कर्ष महत्वपूर्ण प्रशासनिक निर्णयों को प्रभावित कर सकते हैं, अतः जानकारी की सटीकता, विश्वसनीयता तथा सत्यापनशीलता आवश्यक है। उपलब्ध समय सीमित है, इसलिए दिलदार को डेटा का सर्वाधिक विश्वसनीय स्रोत चुनना है।<br>दिलदार को किस स्रोत पर भरोसा करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Viral claims circulating on social media platforms without supporting evidence.","hi":"बिना किसी प्रमाण के सोशल मीडिया पर फैले वायरल दावे।"},"2":{"en":"Personal blogs containing information that has not undergone fact-checking or independent verification.","hi":"ऐसी जानकारी वाले व्यक्तिगत ब्लॉग जिनकी तथ्य-जाँच या स्वतंत्र सत्यापन नहीं हुआ।"},"3":{"en":"Official statistical data released by authorized government agencies through established reporting mechanisms.","hi":"स्थापित रिपोर्टिंग व्यवस्था के माध्यम से अधिकृत सरकारी एजेंसियों द्वारा जारी आधिकारिक सांख्यिकीय आँकड़े।"},"4":{"en":"Anonymous opinions and comments posted on online discussion forums.","hi":"ऑनलाइन चर्चा मंचों पर पोस्ट की गई गुमनाम राय तथा टिप्पणियाँ।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A policy report used for administrative decisions needs data whose source can be checked and trusted<br>Viral claims, unchecked blogs and anonymous comments all lack verification and would make the conclusions weak or misleading<br>Official statistics from authorised government agencies come through a defined reporting system and can be verified, which makes them the reliable source<br>So Dildar should rely on official statistical data<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Official statistical data released by authorized government agencies through established reporting mechanisms..</b>","hi":"नीतिगत निर्णयों में प्रयुक्त रिपोर्ट के लिए ऐसे आँकड़े चाहिए जिनके स्रोत की जाँच और विश्वास किया जा सके<br>वायरल दावे, बिना जाँचे ब्लॉग तथा गुमनाम टिप्पणियाँ सभी सत्यापन से रहित हैं और निष्कर्षों को कमजोर या भ्रामक बना देंगी<br>अधिकृत सरकारी एजेंसियों के आधिकारिक आँकड़े निश्चित रिपोर्टिंग व्यवस्था से आते हैं और सत्यापन योग्य होते हैं, अतः वही विश्वसनीय स्रोत हैं<br>इसलिए दिलदार को आधिकारिक सांख्यिकीय आँकड़ों पर भरोसा करना चाहिए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): स्थापित रिपोर्टिंग व्यवस्था के माध्यम से अधिकृत सरकारी एजेंसियों द्वारा जारी आधिकारिक सांख्यिकीय आँकड़े। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000072002","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question, three statements are given, followed by two conclusions. Consider the statements to be true even if they differ from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions carefully and decide which of the conclusions logically follow from the given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Only a few Cut are Knife.<br>Some Cut are Sharp.<br>No Sharp is Bread.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All Cut are Knife is a possibility.<br>II. All Knife are Cut is a possibility. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में तीन कथन और उनके बाद दो निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न हों। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-से निष्कर्ष दिए गए कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>केवल कुछ Cut, Knife हैं।<br>कुछ Cut, Sharp हैं।<br>कोई Sharp, Bread नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी Cut, Knife हो सकते हैं।<br>II. सभी Knife, Cut हो सकते हैं। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Either conclusion I or conclusion II follows","hi":"या तो निष्कर्ष I या निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Only a few Cut are Knife means that some Cut are Knife and some Cut are definitely not Knife, so all Cut can never be Knife and conclusion I is not a possibility<br>The statements put no restriction on Knife beyond that part, so all Knife being Cut remains possible and conclusion II follows<br>Hence only conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"'केवल कुछ Cut, Knife हैं' का अर्थ है कि कुछ Cut, Knife हैं तथा कुछ Cut निश्चित रूप से Knife नहीं हैं, अतः सभी Cut कभी Knife नहीं हो सकते और निष्कर्ष I संभावना नहीं है<br>कथन उस भाग के अतिरिक्त Knife पर कोई प्रतिबंध नहीं लगाते, अतः सभी Knife के Cut होने की संभावना बनी रहती है और निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000072003","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Choose the alternative which most closely resembles the mirror image of the given combination when MN mirror is placed at the right side of the image.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb36-f744-7f15-86fc-a44a45094051_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008476167\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1] [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए संयोजन के दर्पण प्रतिबिंब से सर्वाधिक मिलता है जब MN दर्पण आकृति के दाईं ओर रखा गया है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019efb36-f744-7f15-86fc-a44a45094051_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150071171\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1] [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb39-28fd-7f47-b558-572fa25a7a6e_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008547520\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f26e4-c232-7dfb-90b1-d8bc47a6e229_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150118836\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb39-28fd-7f47-b558-5730672f34f9_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008612725\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f26e4-c232-7dfb-90b1-d8bd9d302288_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150170562\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb39-28fd-7f47-b558-5731c755662d_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008682136\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f26e4-c232-7dfb-90b1-d8bed6008c8a_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150221330\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb39-28fd-7f47-b558-573268118b02_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008750113\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f26e4-c232-7dfb-90b1-d8bf8c9643ed_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150272312\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"With the mirror on the right, the combination W T P L 5 B 9 # Z is reversed and every character is flipped horizontally at the same height<br>The image must therefore begin with the flipped Z, then #, 9, B, 5, L, P, T and end with the flipped W<br>Only the first option preserves this full reversed order with every character properly flipped<br>Hence the first option is the correct mirror image<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb39-28fd-7f47-b558-572fa25a7a6e_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008547520\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"दर्पण दाईं ओर होने पर संयोजन W T P L 5 B 9 # Z उलट जाता है और प्रत्येक अक्षर उसी ऊँचाई पर क्षैतिज रूप से पलटता है<br>अतः प्रतिबिंब पलटे हुए Z से शुरू होकर #, 9, B, 5, L, P, T तथा अंत में पलटे हुए W पर समाप्त होना चाहिए<br>केवल पहले विकल्प में यह पूरा उलटा क्रम और प्रत्येक अक्षर ठीक से पलटा हुआ है<br>अतः पहला विकल्प सही दर्पण प्रतिबिंब है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f26e4-c232-7dfb-90b1-d8bc47a6e229_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150118836\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb36-f744-7f15-86fc-a44a45094051_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008476167","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019efb36-f744-7f15-86fc-a44a45094051_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150071171"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb39-28fd-7f47-b558-572fa25a7a6e_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008547520","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f26e4-c232-7dfb-90b1-d8bc47a6e229_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150118836"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb39-28fd-7f47-b558-5730672f34f9_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008612725","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f26e4-c232-7dfb-90b1-d8bd9d302288_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150170562"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb39-28fd-7f47-b558-5731c755662d_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008682136","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f26e4-c232-7dfb-90b1-d8bed6008c8a_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150221330"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb39-28fd-7f47-b558-573268118b02_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008750113","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f26e4-c232-7dfb-90b1-d8bf8c9643ed_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150272312"]},"solution":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019efb39-28fd-7f47-b558-572fa25a7a6e_EN.jpg?edu=639294382008547520","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f26e4-c232-7dfb-90b1-d8bc47a6e229_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150118836"]}},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000072004","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"A manufacturing company has implemented predictive maintenance software for its machinery. Which assumption underlies this decision? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक विनिर्माण कंपनी ने अपनी मशीनों के लिए पूर्वानुमानित रखरखाव सॉफ़्टवेयर लागू किया है। इस निर्णय के पीछे कौन-सी अवधारणा निहित है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Employees working on the production floor do not require any training or guidance to operate or understand the predictive maintenance software system.","hi":"उत्पादन तल पर कार्यरत कर्मचारियों को पूर्वानुमानित रखरखाव सॉफ़्टवेयर प्रणाली चलाने या समझने के लिए किसी प्रशिक्षण या मार्गदर्शन की आवश्यकता नहीं है।"},"2":{"en":"Identifying equipment problems before failure can reduce production disruptions and improve overall manufacturing efficiency in the long run.","hi":"विफलता से पहले उपकरण की समस्याओं की पहचान करने से उत्पादन व्यवधान घट सकते हैं तथा लंबे समय में समग्र विनिर्माण दक्षता सुधर सकती है।"},"3":{"en":"Machinery breakdowns will completely stop and never occur again once predictive maintenance software is introduced in the manufacturing process.","hi":"पूर्वानुमानित रखरखाव सॉफ़्टवेयर लागू होने के बाद मशीनरी की खराबी पूरी तरह रुक जाएगी और कभी नहीं होगी।"},"4":{"en":"Software-based predictive maintenance systems are always more effective than experienced maintenance technicians in every possible industrial situation.","hi":"हर संभव औद्योगिक स्थिति में सॉफ़्टवेयर आधारित पूर्वानुमानित रखरखाव प्रणालियाँ अनुभवी रखरखाव तकनीशियनों से सदैव अधिक प्रभावी होती हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Predictive maintenance is installed so that a fault is found before the machine breaks down, which avoids sudden stoppage of production and raises efficiency, and that is exactly the assumption behind the decision<br>The other options promise no training at all, a complete end to breakdowns and a software system always better than every technician, all of which are extreme and unneeded<br>So the assumption is that finding problems before failure reduces disruptions and improves efficiency<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Identifying equipment problems before failure can reduce production disruptions and improve overall manufacturing efficiency in the long run..</b>","hi":"पूर्वानुमानित रखरखाव इसलिए लगाया जाता है कि मशीन खराब होने से पहले गड़बड़ी पकड़ में आ जाए, जिससे उत्पादन का अचानक रुकना टलता है और दक्षता बढ़ती है, और यही निर्णय के पीछे की अवधारणा है<br>अन्य विकल्प किसी प्रशिक्षण की आवश्यकता न होना, खराबी का पूर्ण अंत तथा हर तकनीशियन से सदैव बेहतर सॉफ़्टवेयर का दावा करते हैं, जो अत्यधिक और अनावश्यक हैं<br>अतः अवधारणा यह है कि विफलता से पहले समस्या पकड़ने से व्यवधान घटते हैं और दक्षता सुधरती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): विफलता से पहले उपकरण की समस्याओं की पहचान करने से उत्पादन व्यवधान घट सकते हैं तथा लंबे समय में समग्र विनिर्माण दक्षता सुधर सकती है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000072005","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Select a figure from amongst the Answer Figures which will continue the same series as established by the five Problem Figures.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019f12cb-b72c-7eca-8247-6f57909f3aaf_EN.jpg?edu=639294382009201833\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1] [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पाँच समस्या आकृतियों द्वारा स्थापित उसी श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाने वाली आकृति उत्तर आकृतियों में से चुनिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f12cb-b72c-7eca-8247-6f57909f3aaf_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150619733\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1] [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In every problem figure the two symbols at the top and the two at the bottom are the same pair, and one symbol of the pair changes at every step<br>Tracing the change from A to E, the pair that has to appear in the next figure is the pair of the last step, so the correct figure is the one that keeps this pair in the same corners as the series has been using<br>Answer figure 3 carries this pair in exactly these corners, while the other answer figures repeat a symbol that has already changed or place the symbols in the wrong corners<br>Hence answer figure 3 continues the series<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक समस्या आकृति में ऊपर के दो तथा नीचे के दो चिह्न एक ही युग्म के होते हैं, और प्रत्येक चरण में युग्म का एक चिह्न बदलता है<br>A से E तक परिवर्तन देखने पर अगली आकृति में वही युग्म उन्हीं कोनों में होना चाहिए जो श्रेणी में प्रयुक्त होते आए हैं<br>उत्तर आकृति 3 में यह युग्म ठीक इन्हीं कोनों में है, जबकि अन्य उत्तर आकृतियाँ पहले बदल चुके चिह्न को दोहराती हैं या चिह्नों को गलत कोनों में रखती हैं<br>अतः उत्तर आकृति 3 श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019f12cb-b72c-7eca-8247-6f57909f3aaf_EN.jpg?edu=639294382009201833","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f12cb-b72c-7eca-8247-6f57909f3aaf_HI.jpg?edu=639294382150619733"]}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000072006","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Delhi Sultanate","question":{"en":"Regarding which Sultan did the historian Ziauddin Barani write: \"When he attained Kingship, he was fully independent of the rules and orders of Shariat\"? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"इतिहासकार ज़ियाउद्दीन बरनी ने किस सुल्तान के विषय में लिखा: \"जब उसने राजसत्ता प्राप्त की, तब वह शरियत के नियमों तथा आदेशों से पूर्णतः स्वतंत्र था\"? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Iltutmish","hi":"इल्तुतमिश"},"2":{"en":"Balban","hi":"बलबन"},"3":{"en":"Alauddin Khalji","hi":"अलाउद्दीन खल्जी"},"4":{"en":"Muhammad Bin Tughluq","hi":"मुहम्मद बिन तुगलक"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Alauddin Khalji</b><br>The historian <b>Ziauddin Barani</b>, in his <b>Tarikh-i-Firoz Shahi</b>, wrote this about <b>Alauddin Khalji</b>, whose measures were seen as going beyond the <b>Shariat</b> in matters of state policy.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Alauddin Khalji ruled from <b>1296 to 1316</b> and is known for his <b>market control regulations</b>, land revenue reforms and a large standing army.<br>• He fixed prices of essential commodities, appointed <b>shahana-i-mandi</b> (market controllers) and introduced the <b>dagh</b> (branding of horses) and <b>huliya</b> (descriptive roll of soldiers).<br>• <b>Ziauddin Barani</b> wrote the <b>Tarikh-i-Firoz Shahi</b> and the <b>Fatawa-i-Jahandari</b>, important sources for the Delhi Sultanate.<br>• Barani also wrote about <b>Balban's</b> court etiquette, but the quoted remark on independence from the Shariat refers to Alauddin's administrative decrees.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अलाउद्दीन खल्जी</b><br>इतिहासकार <b>ज़ियाउद्दीन बरनी</b> ने अपनी <b>तारीख-ए-फिरोजशाही</b> में यह बात <b>अलाउद्दीन खल्जी</b> के विषय में लिखी, जिसके राज्य-नीति संबंधी उपाय शरियत से परे माने जाते थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अलाउद्दीन खल्जी ने <b>1296 से 1316</b> तक शासन किया और वह <b>बाजार नियंत्रण नियमों</b>, भू-राजस्व सुधारों तथा विशाल स्थायी सेना के लिए जाना जाता है।<br>• उसने आवश्यक वस्तुओं के मूल्य निर्धारित किए, <b>शाहना-ए-मंडी</b> (बाजार नियंत्रक) नियुक्त किए तथा <b>दाग</b> (घोड़ों पर अंकन) और <b>हुलिया</b> (सैनिकों का विवरण-पत्र) आरंभ किया।<br>• <b>ज़ियाउद्दीन बरनी</b> ने <b>तारीख-ए-फिरोजशाही</b> तथा <b>फतवा-ए-जहांदारी</b> लिखी, जो दिल्ली सल्तनत के महत्वपूर्ण स्रोत हैं।<br>• बरनी ने <b>बलबन</b> के दरबारी शिष्टाचार का भी वर्णन किया, परंतु शरियत से स्वतंत्रता वाला उद्धरण अलाउद्दीन के प्रशासनिक आदेशों से संबंधित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000072007","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Stone Age","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a prominent Mesolithic site located in Rajasthan? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा राजस्थान में स्थित एक प्रमुख मध्यपाषाण स्थल है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chirki Nevasa","hi":"चिरकी नेवासा"},"2":{"en":"Bagor","hi":"बागोर"},"3":{"en":"Didwana","hi":"डीडवाना"},"4":{"en":"Sanghao cave","hi":"संघाओ गुफा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Bagor</b><br><b>Bagor</b>, in <b>Bhilwara district of Rajasthan</b>, is one of the largest and best-excavated <b>Mesolithic sites</b> in India, on the bank of the Kothari river.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bagor shows a long sequence from the <b>Mesolithic to the Chalcolithic and Iron Age</b>, with evidence of microliths, animal domestication and burials.<br>• Important Mesolithic sites in India include <b>Bagor (Rajasthan), Bhimbetka and Adamgarh (Madhya Pradesh), Langhnaj (Gujarat), Teri sites (Tamil Nadu) and Sarai Nahar Rai (Uttar Pradesh)</b>.<br>• <b>Chirki-Nevasa</b> is in <b>Maharashtra</b>, <b>Didwana</b> in Rajasthan has Palaeolithic and salt-lake deposits, and <b>Sanghao cave</b> is in the <b>Potwar plateau</b> of Pakistan.<br>• The Mesolithic period is marked by <b>microliths</b>, hunting-gathering with early domestication, and is dated roughly <b>10,000 to 4,000 BCE</b> in India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बागोर</b><br><b>राजस्थान के भीलवाड़ा जिले</b> में कोठारी नदी के किनारे स्थित <b>बागोर</b> भारत के सबसे बड़े तथा सर्वोत्तम उत्खनित <b>मध्यपाषाण स्थलों</b> में से एक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बागोर में <b>मध्यपाषाण से ताम्रपाषाण तथा लौह युग</b> तक की लंबी परत मिलती है, जिसमें सूक्ष्मपाषाण उपकरण, पशु पालन तथा कब्रों के साक्ष्य हैं।<br>• भारत के प्रमुख मध्यपाषाण स्थलों में <b>बागोर (राजस्थान), भीमबेटका एवं आदमगढ़ (मध्य प्रदेश), लंगनाज (गुजरात), तेरी स्थल (तमिलनाडु) तथा सराय नाहर राय (उत्तर प्रदेश)</b> शामिल हैं।<br>• <b>चिरकी-नेवासा</b> <b>महाराष्ट्र</b> में है, <b>डीडवाना</b> में पुरापाषाण तथा लवण झील निक्षेप हैं, और <b>संघाओ गुफा</b> पाकिस्तान के <b>पोटवार पठार</b> में है।<br>• मध्यपाषाण काल की विशेषता <b>सूक्ष्मपाषाण उपकरण</b> तथा प्रारंभिक पशु पालन सहित शिकार-संग्रह है; भारत में यह लगभग <b>10,000 से 4,000 ईसा पूर्व</b> माना जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000072008","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Northern Plains and Islands","question":{"en":"Which among the following pair of mountain peak and their altitude in the Andaman and Nicobar Islands is <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अंडमान तथा निकोबार द्वीप समूह में पर्वत शिखर और उनकी ऊँचाई के निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा युग्म <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Saddle peak - 742 m","hi":"सैडल पीक - 742 मी"},"2":{"en":"Mount Diavolo - 591 m","hi":"माउंट डियावोलो - 591 मी"},"3":{"en":"Mount Koyob - 476 m","hi":"माउंट कोयोब - 476 मी"},"4":{"en":"Mount Thuiller - 642 m","hi":"माउंट थुइलर - 642 मी"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Mount Thuiller - 642 m</b><br><b>Mount Thuiller</b>, the highest peak of the <b>Great Nicobar Island</b>, has an elevation of about <b>642 metres</b>, so this pair is correctly matched.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Saddle Peak</b> in North Andaman is the <b>highest point of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands</b>, with an elevation of about <b>732 metres</b>, not 742 m.<br>• <b>Mount Diavolo</b> in Middle Andaman is about <b>515 metres</b>, and <b>Mount Koyob</b> in Great Nicobar is about <b>568 metres</b>.<br>• The Andaman and Nicobar Islands form an <b>arc of islands</b> at the junction of the Bay of Bengal and the Andaman Sea, part of a submerged mountain range.<br>• <b>Indira Point</b> on Great Nicobar is the <b>southernmost point of India</b>, and the Ten Degree Channel separates the Andaman and Nicobar groups.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – माउंट थुइलर - 642 मी</b><br><b>ग्रेट निकोबार द्वीप</b> की सर्वोच्च चोटी <b>माउंट थुइलर</b> की ऊँचाई लगभग <b>642 मीटर</b> है, अतः यह युग्म सही सुमेलित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उत्तर अंडमान का <b>सैडल पीक</b> <b>अंडमान तथा निकोबार द्वीप समूह का सर्वोच्च बिंदु</b> है, जिसकी ऊँचाई लगभग <b>732 मीटर</b> है, 742 मी नहीं।<br>• मध्य अंडमान का <b>माउंट डियावोलो</b> लगभग <b>515 मीटर</b> तथा ग्रेट निकोबार का <b>माउंट कोयोब</b> लगभग <b>568 मीटर</b> ऊँचा है।<br>• अंडमान तथा निकोबार द्वीप <b>द्वीपों की चाप</b> बनाते हैं, जो बंगाल की खाड़ी तथा अंडमान सागर के संगम पर एक जलमग्न पर्वत श्रृंखला का भाग है।<br>• ग्रेट निकोबार पर <b>इंदिरा पॉइंट</b> भारत का <b>दक्षिणतम बिंदु</b> है, तथा <b>दस डिग्री चैनल</b> अंडमान और निकोबार समूहों को अलग करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000072009","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"Which statement <b>correctly</b> describes an event occurring at a specific type of plate boundary? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा कथन किसी विशिष्ट प्रकार की प्लेट सीमा पर होने वाली घटना का <b>सही</b> वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"New crust forms at divergent boundaries.","hi":"नई पर्पटी अपसारी सीमाओं पर बनती है।"},"2":{"en":"Trenches form at transform boundaries.","hi":"गर्त संरूपांतर सीमाओं पर बनते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Subduction occurs at divergent boundaries.","hi":"अवपात अपसारी सीमाओं पर होता है।"},"4":{"en":"Plates collide at transform boundaries.","hi":"संरूपांतर सीमाओं पर प्लेटें टकराती हैं।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – New crust forms at divergent boundaries</b><br>At <b>divergent (constructive) boundaries</b> plates move apart and magma rises to fill the gap, so <b>new oceanic crust forms</b>, as at the <b>Mid-Atlantic Ridge</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• At <b>convergent (destructive) boundaries</b> plates collide and one plate <b>subducts</b>, forming <b>trenches, island arcs and fold mountains</b>.<br>• At <b>transform (conservative) boundaries</b> plates slide past each other, producing <b>earthquakes</b> but neither new crust nor trenches, as at the <b>San Andreas Fault</b>.<br>• Divergent boundaries on land form <b>rift valleys</b>, such as the <b>East African Rift</b>, and the <b>Mid-Oceanic Ridge</b> system is the largest such boundary.<br>• The theory of <b>plate tectonics</b> developed from <b>Wegener's continental drift</b> and evidence of <b>sea-floor spreading</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – नई पर्पटी अपसारी सीमाओं पर बनती है।</b><br><b>अपसारी (रचनात्मक) सीमाओं</b> पर प्लेटें दूर हटती हैं और मैग्मा उठकर रिक्त स्थान भरता है, अतः <b>नई महासागरीय पर्पटी बनती है</b>, जैसे <b>मध्य अटलांटिक कटक</b> पर।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अभिसारी (विनाशकारी) सीमाओं</b> पर प्लेटें टकराती हैं और एक प्लेट <b>अवपतित</b> होती है, जिससे <b>गर्त, द्वीप चाप तथा वलित पर्वत</b> बनते हैं।<br>• <b>संरूपांतर (संरक्षी) सीमाओं</b> पर प्लेटें एक-दूसरे के साथ सरकती हैं, जिससे <b>भूकंप</b> तो आते हैं परंतु न नई पर्पटी बनती है न गर्त, जैसे <b>सैन एंड्रियास भ्रंश</b>।<br>• स्थल पर अपसारी सीमाएँ <b>भ्रंश घाटियाँ</b> बनाती हैं, जैसे <b>पूर्वी अफ्रीकी भ्रंश</b>, तथा <b>मध्य महासागरीय कटक</b> तंत्र इस प्रकार की सबसे बड़ी सीमा है।<br>• <b>प्लेट विवर्तनिकी</b> सिद्धांत <b>वेगनर के महाद्वीपीय विस्थापन</b> तथा <b>समुद्र तल प्रसार</b> के प्रमाणों से विकसित हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000072010","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which of the following districts in Maharashtra are known for iron mining? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"महाराष्ट्र के निम्नलिखित में से कौन-से जिले लौह अयस्क खनन के लिए जाने जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mumbai and Pune","hi":"मुंबई तथा पुणे"},"2":{"en":"Nagpur and Nashik","hi":"नागपुर तथा नासिक"},"3":{"en":"Bhandara and Ratnagiri","hi":"भंडारा तथा रत्नागिरी"},"4":{"en":"Aurangabad and Jalgaon","hi":"औरंगाबाद तथा जलगाँव"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Bhandara and Ratnagiri</b><br><b>Bhandara</b> and <b>Ratnagiri</b> districts of Maharashtra are known for <b>iron ore</b> mining, along with Chandrapur and Gadchiroli.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Maharashtra's iron ore occurs mainly in the <b>Dharwar</b> rocks of the eastern Vidarbha region and the Konkan belt.<br>• The state is also a major producer of <b>manganese, bauxite and coal</b>, the coal coming from the <b>Wardha valley</b> and Vidarbha coalfields.<br>• Leading iron ore producing states in India are <b>Odisha, Chhattisgarh, Karnataka, Jharkhand and Goa</b>, with major belts at <b>Barbil, Bailadila, Bellary and Kudremukh</b>.<br>• <b>Ratnagiri</b> is also famous for <b>alfonso mangoes</b>, and iron ore from the Konkan was historically exported through Redi and Dighi ports.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – भंडारा तथा रत्नागिरी</b><br>महाराष्ट्र के <b>भंडारा</b> तथा <b>रत्नागिरी</b> जिले <b>लौह अयस्क</b> खनन के लिए जाने जाते हैं, साथ में चंद्रपुर एवं गडचिरोली भी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• महाराष्ट्र में लौह अयस्क मुख्यतः पूर्वी विदर्भ के <b>धारवाड़</b> शैलों तथा कोंकण पट्टी में मिलता है।<br>• राज्य <b>मैंगनीज, बॉक्साइट तथा कोयले</b> का भी प्रमुख उत्पादक है; कोयला <b>वर्धा घाटी</b> तथा विदर्भ कोयला क्षेत्रों से आता है।<br>• भारत के प्रमुख लौह अयस्क उत्पादक राज्य <b>ओडिशा, छत्तीसगढ़, कर्नाटक, झारखंड तथा गोवा</b> हैं, जहाँ <b>बारबिल, बैलाडीला, बेल्लारी तथा कुद्रेमुख</b> प्रमुख पट्टियाँ हैं।<br>• <b>रत्नागिरी</b> <b>अल्फांसो आम</b> के लिए भी प्रसिद्ध है तथा कोंकण का लौह अयस्क ऐतिहासिक रूप से रेडी तथा दीघी बंदरगाहों से निर्यात होता था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000072011","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"The festival of Maghe Sankranti is primarily celebrated in which of the following states? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"माघे संक्रांति का उत्सव मुख्यतः निम्नलिखित में से किस राज्य में मनाया जाता है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Assam","hi":"असम"},"2":{"en":"Sikkim","hi":"सिक्किम"},"3":{"en":"Mizoram","hi":"मिजोरम"},"4":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sikkim</b><br><b>Maghe Sankranti</b> is celebrated mainly in <b>Sikkim</b> (and in Nepal) in the month of <b>Magh (January)</b>, marking the <b>winter solstice transition</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The festival is observed by the <b>Nepali community</b> of Sikkim, who take holy dips in rivers and eat <b>til (sesame), ghee, sweet potato and yam</b>.<br>• It is also called <b>Maghe Sankranti or Makar Sankranti</b> and marks the sun's northward journey (<b>Uttarayan</b>).<br>• Similar festivals elsewhere are <b>Makar Sankranti (Gujarat and Maharashtra), Pongal (Tamil Nadu), Bihu (Assam), Maghi (Punjab) and Khichdi Parv (Bihar)</b>.<br>• Sikkim's other festivals include <b>Losar, Saga Dawa, Pang-Lhabsol and Losoong</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सिक्किम</b><br><b>माघे संक्रांति</b> मुख्यतः <b>सिक्किम</b> (तथा नेपाल) में <b>माघ मास (जनवरी)</b> में मनाई जाती है और यह <b>शीतकालीन अयनांत परिवर्तन</b> का प्रतीक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह उत्सव सिक्किम के <b>नेपाली समुदाय</b> द्वारा मनाया जाता है, जो नदियों में पवित्र स्नान करते हैं तथा <b>तिल, घी, शकरकंद तथा जिमीकंद</b> खाते हैं।<br>• इसे <b>माघे संक्रांति अथवा मकर संक्रांति</b> भी कहते हैं और यह सूर्य के उत्तरायण होने का प्रतीक है।<br>• अन्यत्र इसी प्रकार के उत्सव <b>मकर संक्रांति (गुजरात तथा महाराष्ट्र), पोंगल (तमिलनाडु), बिहू (असम), माघी (पंजाब) तथा खिचड़ी पर्व (बिहार)</b> हैं।<br>• सिक्किम के अन्य उत्सव <b>लोसार, सागा दावा, पांग-ल्हाबसोल तथा लोसूंग</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000072012","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Ravi Agrawal is the head of which tax administration body in 2026? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2026 में रवि अग्रवाल किस कर प्रशासन निकाय के प्रमुख हैं? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs","hi":"केंद्रीय अप्रत्यक्ष कर तथा सीमा शुल्क बोर्ड"},"2":{"en":"Central Board of Direct Taxes","hi":"केंद्रीय प्रत्यक्ष कर बोर्ड"},"3":{"en":"Goods and Services Tax (GST) Network","hi":"वस्तु एवं सेवा कर (जीएसटी) नेटवर्क"},"4":{"en":"Income Tax Appellate Tribunal","hi":"आयकर अपीलीय अधिकरण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Central Board of Direct Taxes</b><br><b>Ravi Agrawal</b> is the <b>Chairman of the Central Board of Direct Taxes (CBDT)</b>, the apex body for <b>direct tax</b> administration in India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>CBDT</b> functions under the <b>Central Board of Revenue Act, 1963</b> and administers the <b>Income Tax Act, 1961</b>.<br>• The <b>Central Board of Indirect Taxes and Customs (CBIC)</b> handles <b>GST, customs and excise</b>, and both boards are under the <b>Ministry of Finance</b>.<br>• The CBDT is headed by a <b>Chairman</b> and consists of <b>Members</b> in charge of different functional areas such as legislation, administration and audit.<br>• The <b>GST Network (GSTN)</b> is a not-for-profit company that runs the GST IT platform, and the <b>ITAT</b> is an appellate tribunal.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केंद्रीय प्रत्यक्ष कर बोर्ड</b><br><b>रवि अग्रवाल</b> भारत में <b>प्रत्यक्ष कर</b> प्रशासन के सर्वोच्च निकाय <b>केंद्रीय प्रत्यक्ष कर बोर्ड (CBDT)</b> के <b>अध्यक्ष</b> हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>CBDT</b> <b>केंद्रीय राजस्व अधिनियम, 1963</b> के अंतर्गत कार्य करता है तथा <b>आयकर अधिनियम, 1961</b> का प्रशासन देखता है।<br>• <b>केंद्रीय अप्रत्यक्ष कर तथा सीमा शुल्क बोर्ड (CBIC)</b> <b>जीएसटी, सीमा शुल्क तथा उत्पाद शुल्क</b> देखता है; दोनों बोर्ड <b>वित्त मंत्रालय</b> के अधीन हैं।<br>• CBDT का प्रमुख <b>अध्यक्ष</b> होता है तथा इसमें विधान, प्रशासन तथा लेखा-परीक्षा जैसे कार्यक्षेत्रों के <b>सदस्य</b> होते हैं।<br>• <b>जीएसटी नेटवर्क (GSTN)</b> एक लाभ-रहित कंपनी है जो जीएसटी आईटी प्लेटफॉर्म चलाती है, और <b>ITAT</b> एक अपीलीय अधिकरण है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000072013","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"Which Harappan site is especially noted for extensive stone construction? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा हड़प्पा स्थल विस्तृत पाषाण निर्माण के लिए विशेष रूप से उल्लेखनीय है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Harappa","hi":"हड़प्पा"},"2":{"en":"Mohenjo-daro","hi":"मोहनजोदड़ो"},"3":{"en":"Kalibangan","hi":"कालीबंगा"},"4":{"en":"Dholavira","hi":"धोलावीरा"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Dholavira</b><br><b>Dholavira</b> in <b>Kachchh, Gujarat</b>, is noted for its extensive use of <b>stone</b> in construction, unlike most Harappan sites that used <b>burnt and mud bricks</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Dholavira had a <b>three-part division</b> - the <b>citadel, the middle town and the lower town</b> - enclosed by massive stone walls and gateways.<br>• It is famous for its <b>water reservoirs</b>, a sophisticated <b>water harvesting system</b>, the <b>signboard with the Indus script</b> and a large stadium-like ground.<br>• Dholavira was declared a <b>UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2021</b> and is one of the finest examples of Harappan town planning and hydraulic engineering.<br>• <b>Harappa</b> and <b>Mohenjo-daro</b> were built largely of <b>unburnt and burnt bricks</b>, and <b>Kalibangan</b> is known for its <b>ploughed field and fire altars</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – धोलावीरा</b><br><b>गुजरात के कच्छ</b> में स्थित <b>धोलावीरा</b> निर्माण में <b>पत्थर</b> के विस्तृत उपयोग के लिए उल्लेखनीय है, जबकि अधिकांश हड़प्पा स्थलों में <b>पक्की तथा कच्ची ईंटें</b> प्रयुक्त हुईं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• धोलावीरा <b>तीन भागों</b> - <b>गढ़ी, मध्य नगर तथा निचला नगर</b> - में विभाजित था, जो विशाल पाषाण दीवारों तथा प्रवेश-द्वारों से घिरा था।<br>• यह अपने <b>जलाशयों</b>, विकसित <b>जल संचयन प्रणाली</b>, <b>सिंधु लिपि वाले साइनबोर्ड</b> तथा विशाल स्टेडियम जैसे मैदान के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।<br>• धोलावीरा को <b>2021 में यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल</b> घोषित किया गया और यह हड़प्पा नगर नियोजन तथा जल अभियांत्रिकी का श्रेष्ठ उदाहरण है।<br>• <b>हड़प्पा</b> तथा <b>मोहनजोदड़ो</b> मुख्यतः <b>कच्ची एवं पक्की ईंटों</b> से बने थे, तथा <b>कालीबंगा</b> <b>जुते खेत तथा अग्नि वेदियों</b> के लिए जाना जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000072014","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"In India, Justice Dinesh Maheshwari was appointed in April 2025 to head which high-level advisory body responsible for recommending legal reforms? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में अप्रैल 2025 में न्यायमूर्ति दिनेश माहेश्वरी को किस उच्च स्तरीय सलाहकार निकाय का प्रमुख नियुक्त किया गया, जो विधिक सुधारों की सिफारिश करने हेतु उत्तरदायी है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Law Commission of India","hi":"भारत विधि आयोग"},"2":{"en":"Finance Commission of India","hi":"भारत वित्त आयोग"},"3":{"en":"National Judicial Commission","hi":"राष्ट्रीय न्यायिक आयोग"},"4":{"en":"Central Vigilance Commission","hi":"केंद्रीय सतर्कता आयोग"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Law Commission of India</b><br>In <b>April 2025</b>, former Supreme Court judge <b>Justice Dinesh Maheshwari</b> was appointed <b>Chairperson of the Law Commission of India</b>, the body that recommends legal reforms.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Law Commission of India</b> is an <b>executive body</b>, not a constitutional or statutory one, constituted by the <b>Ministry of Law and Justice</b> for a fixed term.<br>• Its main function is to <b>review existing laws</b> and recommend <b>reforms, repeal of obsolete laws and new legislation</b>.<br>• The first Law Commission was constituted in <b>1955</b> with <b>M.C. Setalvad</b> as chairman, and the <b>22nd Law Commission</b> is the current one.<br>• The <b>Finance Commission</b> is constituted under <b>Article 280</b>, the <b>National Judicial Appointments Commission</b> was struck down in 2015, and the <b>CVC</b> is a statutory body under the CVC Act, 2003.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – भारत विधि आयोग</b><br><b>अप्रैल 2025</b> में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के पूर्व न्यायाधीश <b>न्यायमूर्ति दिनेश माहेश्वरी</b> को <b>भारत विधि आयोग</b> का <b>अध्यक्ष</b> नियुक्त किया गया, जो विधिक सुधारों की सिफारिश करने वाला निकाय है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>भारत विधि आयोग</b> <b>कार्यकारी निकाय</b> है, संवैधानिक अथवा सांविधिक नहीं; इसे <b>विधि एवं न्याय मंत्रालय</b> निश्चित अवधि के लिए गठित करता है।<br>• इसका मुख्य कार्य <b>विद्यमान विधियों का पुनरावलोकन</b> करना तथा <b>सुधार, अप्रचलित विधियों का निरसन एवं नई विधि</b> की सिफारिश करना है।<br>• प्रथम विधि आयोग <b>1955</b> में <b>एम.सी. सीतलवाड़</b> की अध्यक्षता में गठित हुआ, तथा वर्तमान में <b>22वाँ विधि आयोग</b> है।<br>• <b>वित्त आयोग</b> <b>अनुच्छेद 280</b> के अंतर्गत गठित होता है, <b>राष्ट्रीय न्यायिक नियुक्ति आयोग</b> 2015 में निरस्त किया गया, तथा <b>CVC</b> CVC अधिनियम, 2003 के अंतर्गत सांविधिक निकाय है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000072015","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Defence News","question":{"en":"Under the Agnipath Scheme in India, what is the initial tenure of service for an Agniveer? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में अग्निपथ योजना के अंतर्गत अग्निवीर के लिए सेवा की प्रारंभिक अवधि क्या है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2 years","hi":"2 वर्ष"},"2":{"en":"4 years","hi":"4 वर्ष"},"3":{"en":"5 years","hi":"5 वर्ष"},"4":{"en":"10 years","hi":"10 वर्ष"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 4 years</b><br>Under the <b>Agnipath Scheme</b>, an <b>Agniveer</b> is enrolled for an initial tenure of <b>4 years</b> in the armed forces.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The scheme was launched in <b>June 2022</b> for recruitment to the <b>Army, Navy and Air Force</b> below officer rank.<br>• After the 4-year engagement, up to <b>25% of each batch</b> may be retained in regular service based on merit, and the rest get a <b>Seva Nidhi package</b>.<br>• Agniveers receive <b>skill training, a monthly package and insurance cover</b>, and recruitment is conducted through the <b>Agniveer Vayu, Agniveer (Army) and SSR/ MR</b> entry schemes.<br>• The scheme was challenged in courts and the Supreme Court upheld it, while directing that <b>skill certificates and medical facilities</b> be provided.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 4 वर्ष</b><br><b>अग्निपथ योजना</b> के अंतर्गत <b>अग्निवीर</b> की सशस्त्र बलों में <b>4 वर्ष</b> की प्रारंभिक अवधि के लिए भर्ती होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह योजना <b>जून 2022</b> में <b>सेना, नौसेना तथा वायुसेना</b> में अधिकारी रैंक से नीचे भर्ती हेतु आरंभ की गई।<br>• 4 वर्ष की सेवा के बाद प्रत्येक बैच के <b>25% तक</b> अग्निवीरों को योग्यता के आधार पर नियमित सेवा में रखा जा सकता है, तथा शेष को <b>सेवा निधि पैकेज</b> मिलता है।<br>• अग्निवीरों को <b>कौशल प्रशिक्षण, मासिक पैकेज तथा बीमा</b> मिलता है, और भर्ती <b>अग्निवीर वायु, अग्निवीर (सेना) तथा SSR/MR</b> योजनाओं से होती है।<br>• इस योजना को न्यायालयों में चुनौती दी गई तथा सर्वोच्च न्यायालय ने इसे वैध ठहराया, साथ ही <b>कौशल प्रमाणपत्र तथा चिकित्सा सुविधाएँ</b> देने का निर्देश दिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000072016","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Who wrote \"Dada Seerisu Tande\", the short story collection that won the Sahitya Akademi Award 2025? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\"दादा सीरिसु तांदे\" कहानी-संग्रह के लेखक कौन हैं, जिसने साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025 प्राप्त किया? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Haobam Nalini","hi":"हाओबाम नलिनी"},"2":{"en":"Amaresh Nugadoni","hi":"अमरेश नुगदोनी"},"3":{"en":"Bhagwan Atlani","hi":"भगवान अटलानी"},"4":{"en":"Jitender Kumar Soni","hi":"जितेंद्र कुमार सोनी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Amaresh Nugadoni</b><br><b>Amaresh Nugadoni</b> wrote <b>Dada Seerisu Tande</b>, the <b>short story collection</b> that won the <b>Sahitya Akademi Award 2025</b> in <b>Kannada</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Sahitya Akademi Award</b> is conferred annually for outstanding literary work in each of the languages recognised by the Akademi.<br>• <b>Kannada</b> is a Dravidian language listed in the <b>Eighth Schedule</b>, and writers such as <b>Kuvempu, D.R. Bendre and Girish Karnad</b> have won national literary honours.<br>• The award carries a <b>casket, a plaque and a cash prize</b> and is announced along with the <b>Yuva Puraskar and Bal Sahitya Puraskar</b>.<br>• The highest literary honour in India, the <b>Jnanpith</b>, has been awarded to <b>eight Kannada writers</b>, the most for any language.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अमरेश नुगदोनी</b><br><b>अमरेश नुगदोनी</b> ने <b>दादा सीरिसु तांदे</b> लिखी, जो <b>कन्नड़</b> में <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार 2025</b> प्राप्त करने वाला <b>कहानी-संग्रह</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार</b> प्रत्येक वर्ष अकादमी द्वारा मान्य भाषाओं में उत्कृष्ट साहित्यिक कृति पर दिया जाता है।<br>• <b>कन्नड़</b> द्रविड़ भाषा है जो <b>आठवीं अनुसूची</b> में है, तथा <b>कुवेंपु, डी.आर. बेंद्रे तथा गिरीश कर्नाड</b> जैसे लेखकों को राष्ट्रीय साहित्यिक सम्मान मिले हैं।<br>• पुरस्कार में <b>पत्रिका, ताम्रपत्र तथा नकद राशि</b> मिलती है और इसकी घोषणा <b>युवा पुरस्कार एवं बाल साहित्य पुरस्कार</b> के साथ होती है।<br>• भारत का सर्वोच्च साहित्यिक सम्मान <b>ज्ञानपीठ</b> <b>आठ कन्नड़ लेखकों</b> को मिला है, जो किसी भी भाषा के लिए सर्वाधिक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000072017","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Himalayan River System","question":{"en":"The river Barak is an important river of: [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बराक नदी किसकी एक महत्वपूर्ण नदी है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Manipur, Mizoram, and Assam","hi":"मणिपुर, मिजोरम तथा असम"},"2":{"en":"Assam, Tripura and Manipur","hi":"असम, त्रिपुरा तथा मणिपुर"},"3":{"en":"Nagaland, Arunachal Pradesh and Assam","hi":"नगालैंड, अरुणाचल प्रदेश तथा असम"},"4":{"en":"Tripura, Nagaland and Assam","hi":"त्रिपुरा, नगालैंड तथा असम"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Manipur, Mizoram, and Assam</b><br>The <b>Barak</b> rises in the <b>Manipur hills</b>, flows through <b>Mizoram</b> and <b>southern Assam</b>, and then enters Bangladesh as the <b>Surma-Kushiyara</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Barak is the <b>second largest river of the north-east</b> after the Brahmaputra and drains the <b>Barak valley</b> of Assam, whose main towns are <b>Silchar, Karimganj and Cachar</b>.<br>• Its major tributaries include the <b>Jiri, Dhaleswari, Singla, Longai and Katakhal</b>, and it splits into the <b>Surma and Kushiyara</b> in Bangladesh.<br>• The Barak valley is part of the <b>Surma-Meghna basin</b>, and the river finally joins the <b>Meghna</b>, which flows into the Bay of Bengal.<br>• The Brahmaputra and the Barak are separated by the <b>Meghalaya plateau and the Barail range</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मणिपुर, मिजोरम तथा असम</b><br><b>बराक</b> <b>मणिपुर की पहाड़ियों</b> से निकलती है, <b>मिजोरम</b> तथा <b>दक्षिणी असम</b> से बहती है और फिर बांग्लादेश में <b>सुरमा-कुशियारा</b> के रूप में प्रवेश करती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बराक ब्रह्मपुत्र के बाद <b>पूर्वोत्तर की दूसरी सबसे बड़ी नदी</b> है और असम की <b>बराक घाटी</b> को अपवाहित करती है, जिसके प्रमुख नगर <b>सिलचर, करीमगंज तथा कछार</b> हैं।<br>• इसकी प्रमुख सहायक नदियाँ <b>जिरी, धलेश्वरी, सिंगला, लोंगई तथा कटखल</b> हैं, तथा बांग्लादेश में यह <b>सुरमा और कुशियारा</b> में विभाजित होती है।<br>• बराक घाटी <b>सुरमा-मेघना बेसिन</b> का भाग है और यह अंततः <b>मेघना</b> में मिलकर बंगाल की खाड़ी में गिरती है।<br>• ब्रह्मपुत्र तथा बराक <b>मेघालय पठार एवं बरैल श्रेणी</b> द्वारा अलग होती हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000072018","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"Under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India, which of the following would not amount to an \"offence\" as defined under Section 2(24)? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कार्य धारा 2(24) के अंतर्गत परिभाषित \"अपराध\" नहीं होगा? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"An act committed by a person under seven years of age","hi":"सात वर्ष से कम आयु के व्यक्ति द्वारा किया गया कार्य"},"2":{"en":"An act punishable under BNS (Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita) with imprisonment","hi":"भारतीय न्याय संहिता के अंतर्गत कारावास से दंडनीय कार्य"},"3":{"en":"An act punishable under a local law with six months imprisonment","hi":"स्थानीय विधि के अंतर्गत छह माह के कारावास से दंडनीय कार्य"},"4":{"en":"An act causing harm due to negligence","hi":"लापरवाही से हानि पहुँचाने वाला कार्य"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – An act committed by a person under seven years of age</b><br>Section <b>2(24)</b> of the <b>BNS, 2023</b> defines \"offence\", but an act by a child <b>under seven years of age</b> is excluded from criminal liability under the general exceptions, so it does not amount to an offence.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>BNS</b> provides that nothing done by a child <b>under seven years</b> is an offence, and for children between <b>seven and twelve</b> years the act is excused if the child has not attained sufficient maturity of understanding.<br>• An \"offence\" means an act made punishable by the <b>BNS</b> or by any <b>special or local law</b>.<br>• Acts punishable with imprisonment under the BNS or a local law are offences, and acts causing harm negligently are punishable under provisions such as those on <b>negligent conduct</b>.<br>• The <b>BNS</b> replaced the <b>Indian Penal Code, 1860</b> and came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – सात वर्ष से कम आयु के व्यक्ति द्वारा किया गया कार्य</b><br><b>BNS, 2023</b> की धारा <b>2(24)</b> \"अपराध\" को परिभाषित करती है, परंतु <b>सात वर्ष से कम आयु</b> के बच्चे द्वारा किया गया कार्य सामान्य अपवादों के अंतर्गत आपराधिक दायित्व से बाहर है, अतः वह अपराध नहीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>BNS</b> में प्रावधान है कि <b>सात वर्ष से कम</b> आयु के बच्चे द्वारा किया गया कार्य अपराध नहीं है, तथा <b>सात से बारह वर्ष</b> के बच्चों के लिए यदि उनमें पर्याप्त समझ नहीं है तो कार्य क्षम्य है।<br>• \"अपराध\" का अर्थ <b>BNS</b> अथवा किसी <b>विशेष या स्थानीय विधि</b> द्वारा दंडनीय कार्य है।<br>• BNS अथवा स्थानीय विधि के अंतर्गत कारावास से दंडनीय कार्य अपराध हैं, तथा लापरवाही से हानि पहुँचाने वाले कार्य <b>लापरवाह आचरण</b> संबंधी प्रावधानों के अंतर्गत दंडनीय हैं।<br>• <b>BNS</b> ने <b>भारतीय दंड संहिता, 1860</b> का स्थान लिया और यह <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से प्रभावी हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000072019","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who was appointed as the Acting Chairperson of the National Human Rights Commission (NHRC) of India with effect from June 2024? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जून 2024 से प्रभावी रूप से भारत के राष्ट्रीय मानवाधिकार आयोग (NHRC) की कार्यवाहक अध्यक्ष के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Justice Arun Mishra","hi":"न्यायमूर्ति अरुण मिश्रा"},"2":{"en":"Vijaya Bharathi Sayani","hi":"विजया भारती सायानी"},"3":{"en":"Justice H.L. Dattu","hi":"न्यायमूर्ति एच.एल. दत्तू"},"4":{"en":"Rajiv Jain","hi":"राजीव जैन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Vijaya Bharathi Sayani</b><br><b>Vijaya Bharathi Sayani</b> took over as the <b>Acting Chairperson of the NHRC</b> with effect from <b>June 2024</b>, following the completion of the term of Justice Arun Mishra.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>NHRC</b> is a statutory body established under the <b>Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993</b>, and functions as the watchdog of human rights in India.<br>• It consists of a <b>Chairperson</b>, a number of <b>Members</b> and <b>ex-officio members</b>, and the Chairperson is appointed by the <b>President</b> on the recommendation of a committee of the Prime Minister, the Speaker, the Home Minister, the Leaders of Opposition in both Houses and the Deputy Chairman of the Rajya Sabha.<br>• The Chairperson is usually a former <b>Chief Justice or judge of the Supreme Court</b>, and the body has recommendatory powers only.<br>• <b>Justice H.L. Dattu</b> and <b>Justice Arun Mishra</b> are former chairpersons of the NHRC.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – विजया भारती सायानी</b><br><b>विजया भारती सायानी</b> ने न्यायमूर्ति अरुण मिश्रा का कार्यकाल पूरा होने पर <b>जून 2024</b> से <b>NHRC की कार्यवाहक अध्यक्ष</b> का पदभार संभाला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>NHRC</b> <b>मानव अधिकार संरक्षण अधिनियम, 1993</b> के अंतर्गत स्थापित सांविधिक निकाय है और भारत में मानवाधिकारों की निगरानी करता है।<br>• इसमें एक <b>अध्यक्ष</b>, कई <b>सदस्य</b> तथा <b>पदेन सदस्य</b> होते हैं; अध्यक्ष को <b>राष्ट्रपति</b> प्रधानमंत्री, अध्यक्ष, गृह मंत्री, दोनों सदनों के विपक्ष के नेता तथा राज्यसभा के उपसभापति की समिति की सिफारिश पर नियुक्त करता है।<br>• अध्यक्ष सामान्यतः सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के पूर्व <b>मुख्य न्यायाधीश अथवा न्यायाधीश</b> होते हैं, तथा यह निकाय केवल सिफारिशी शक्तियाँ रखता है।<br>• <b>न्यायमूर्ति एच.एल. दत्तू</b> तथा <b>न्यायमूर्ति अरुण मिश्रा</b> NHRC के पूर्व अध्यक्ष हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000072020","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Socio Religious Reforms","question":{"en":"Which Indian social reformer worked for leprosy patients and founded Anandwan? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस भारतीय समाज सुधारक ने कुष्ठ रोगियों के लिए कार्य किया तथा आनंदवन की स्थापना की? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Baba Amte","hi":"बाबा आमटे"},"2":{"en":"Vinoba Bhave","hi":"विनोबा भावे"},"3":{"en":"Jayaprakash Narayan","hi":"जयप्रकाश नारायण"},"4":{"en":"E. V. Ramasamy","hi":"ई. वी. रामासामी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Baba Amte</b><br><b>Baba Amte</b> founded <b>Anandwan</b> in <b>Chandrapur district of Maharashtra</b> in <b>1949</b> as a self-sufficient settlement for people affected by <b>leprosy</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• His organisation, <b>Maharogi Sewa Samiti</b>, runs <b>Anandwan, Hemalkasa and Somnath</b> projects for leprosy patients, tribal people and the disabled.<br>• He was awarded the <b>Ramon Magsaysay Award in 1985</b>, the <b>Padma Shri</b>, the <b>Padma Vibhushan in 1986</b> and the <b>Gandhi Peace Prize</b>.<br>• He was also associated with the <b>Narmada Bachao Andolan</b> and campaigns against dam displacement and nuclear weapons.<br>• <b>Vinoba Bhave</b> led the <b>Bhoodan movement</b>, <b>Jayaprakash Narayan</b> led the <b>Sampoorna Kranti</b> movement, and <b>E.V. Ramasamy (Periyar)</b> led the <b>Self-Respect Movement</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – बाबा आमटे</b><br><b>बाबा आमटे</b> ने <b>1949</b> में <b>महाराष्ट्र के चंद्रपुर जिले</b> में <b>कुष्ठ रोग</b> से प्रभावित लोगों के लिए आत्मनिर्भर बस्ती के रूप में <b>आनंदवन</b> की स्थापना की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उनकी संस्था <b>महारोगी सेवा समिति</b> कुष्ठ रोगियों, जनजातीय लोगों तथा दिव्यांगों के लिए <b>आनंदवन, हेमलकसा तथा सोमनाथ</b> परियोजनाएँ चलाती है।<br>• उन्हें <b>1985 में रेमन मैग्सेसे पुरस्कार</b>, <b>पद्म श्री</b>, <b>1986 में पद्म विभूषण</b> तथा <b>गांधी शांति पुरस्कार</b> मिला।<br>• वे <b>नर्मदा बचाओ आंदोलन</b> तथा बाँध विस्थापन एवं परमाणु हथियारों के विरुद्ध अभियानों से भी जुड़े रहे।<br>• <b>विनोबा भावे</b> ने <b>भूदान आंदोलन</b>, <b>जयप्रकाश नारायण</b> ने <b>संपूर्ण क्रांति</b> तथा <b>ई.वी. रामासामी (पेरियार)</b> ने <b>स्वाभिमान आंदोलन</b> का नेतृत्व किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000072021","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Post-Maurya Dynasties","question":{"en":"Which type of stone was predominantly utilized by craftsmen of the early Gandhara school of sculptural art? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"गांधार मूर्तिकला शैली के प्रारंभिक काल में शिल्पकारों ने मुख्यतः किस प्रकार के पत्थर का उपयोग किया? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Blue-grey schist stone","hi":"नीले-धूसर शिस्ट पत्थर"},"2":{"en":"Spotted red sandstone","hi":"चितकबरा लाल बलुआ पत्थर"},"3":{"en":"White crystalline marble","hi":"श्वेत क्रिस्टलीय संगमरमर"},"4":{"en":"Buff Chunar sandstone","hi":"पीला चुनार बलुआ पत्थर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Blue-grey schist stone</b><br>The early <b>Gandhara school</b> of sculpture used mainly <b>blue-grey schist</b> from the Peshawar region, and later used <b>stucco</b> as well.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Gandhara school flourished in the <b>north-west</b> (present-day Pakistan and Afghanistan) under the <b>Kushanas</b> and <b>Shakas</b>, and shows strong <b>Hellenistic and Roman</b> influence.<br>• Its distinctive features include <b>realistic drapery, curly hair, wavy folds and the halo</b> around Buddha, modelled on Greek and Roman art.<br>• The <b>Mathura school</b> used <b>spotted red sandstone</b>, and the <b>Amaravati school</b> used <b>white crystalline marble</b>.<br>• <b>Chunar sandstone</b> was used for the <b>Mauryan pillars</b> and polished surfaces, not for Gandhara images.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – नीले-धूसर शिस्ट पत्थर</b><br>प्रारंभिक <b>गांधार शैली</b> की मूर्तिकला में मुख्यतः पेशावर क्षेत्र का <b>नीला-धूसर शिस्ट</b> प्रयुक्त हुआ, तथा बाद में <b>स्टक्को</b> का भी उपयोग हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गांधार शैली <b>उत्तर-पश्चिम</b> (वर्तमान पाकिस्तान तथा अफगानिस्तान) में <b>कुषाणों</b> तथा <b>शकों</b> के अधीन विकसित हुई और इसमें <b>यूनानी एवं रोमन</b> प्रभाव स्पष्ट है।<br>• इसकी विशेषताएँ <b>यथार्थवादी वस्त्राभरण, घुंघराले केश, लहरदार वलियाँ तथा बुद्ध के चारों ओर प्रभामंडल</b> हैं, जो ग्रीक-रोमन कला से प्रेरित हैं।<br>• <b>मथुरा शैली</b> में <b>चितकबरा लाल बलुआ पत्थर</b> तथा <b>अमरावती शैली</b> में <b>श्वेत क्रिस्टलीय संगमरमर</b> प्रयुक्त हुआ।<br>• <b>चुनार बलुआ पत्थर</b> <b>मौर्य स्तंभों</b> तथा चमकदार सतहों के लिए प्रयुक्त हुआ, गांधार प्रतिमाओं के लिए नहीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000072022","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"After the 1991 reforms, which sector continued to remain reserved for the public sector? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 के सुधारों के बाद कौन-सा क्षेत्र सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के लिए आरक्षित बना रहा? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Consumer goods and Railway Transport","hi":"उपभोक्ता वस्तुएँ तथा रेल परिवहन"},"2":{"en":"Atomic energy and Railway Transport","hi":"परमाणु ऊर्जा तथा रेल परिवहन"},"3":{"en":"Textile industry and Automobile sector","hi":"वस्त्र उद्योग तथा ऑटोमोबाइल क्षेत्र"},"4":{"en":"Automobile sector and Atomic energy","hi":"ऑटोमोबाइल क्षेत्र तथा परमाणु ऊर्जा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Atomic energy and Railway Transport</b><br>The <b>New Industrial Policy of 1991</b> reduced the number of industries reserved for the public sector from <b>17 to 8</b>, and <b>atomic energy and railway transport</b> remained reserved.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The industries retained in the public sector included <b>atomic energy, defence production, mining of certain minerals, and railway transport</b>.<br>• Later, <b>mining of iron ore, manganese, chrome, gypsum, sulphur, gold, diamonds, copper and zinc</b> was also opened to private participation.<br>• The 1991 policy <b>abolished industrial licensing</b> for most industries, removed <b>MRTP restrictions</b> and allowed <b>foreign direct investment</b>.<br>• The policy was announced along with the <b>devaluation of the rupee</b> and reforms of the <b>trade and financial sectors</b> during the balance of payments crisis.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – परमाणु ऊर्जा तथा रेल परिवहन</b><br><b>1991 की नई औद्योगिक नीति</b> ने सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के लिए आरक्षित उद्योगों की संख्या <b>17 से घटाकर 8</b> कर दी, तथा <b>परमाणु ऊर्जा और रेल परिवहन</b> आरक्षित रहे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र में रखे गए उद्योगों में <b>परमाणु ऊर्जा, रक्षा उत्पादन, कुछ खनिजों का खनन तथा रेल परिवहन</b> शामिल थे।<br>• बाद में <b>लौह अयस्क, मैंगनीज, क्रोम, जिप्सम, सल्फर, स्वर्ण, हीरा, तांबा तथा जस्ता</b> के खनन को भी निजी भागीदारी हेतु खोल दिया गया।<br>• 1991 की नीति ने अधिकांश उद्योगों की <b>औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग समाप्त</b> की, <b>एमआरटीपी प्रतिबंध</b> हटाए तथा <b>प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश</b> की अनुमति दी।<br>• यह नीति भुगतान संतुलन संकट के दौरान <b>रुपये के अवमूल्यन</b> तथा <b>व्यापार एवं वित्तीय क्षेत्र</b> के सुधारों के साथ घोषित की गई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000072023","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which venue hosted the India Open Super 750 badminton tournament held from 13-18 January 2026? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"13-18 जनवरी 2026 तक आयोजित इंडिया ओपन सुपर 750 बैडमिंटन प्रतियोगिता का आयोजन स्थल कौन-सा था? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Indira Gandhi Arena, New Delhi","hi":"इंदिरा गांधी एरीना, नई दिल्ली"},"2":{"en":"Babu Banarasi Das Indoor Stadium, Lucknow","hi":"बाबू बनारसी दास इंडोर स्टेडियम, लखनऊ"},"3":{"en":"Kanteerava Indoor Stadium, Bengaluru","hi":"कंटीरवा इंडोर स्टेडियम, बेंगलुरु"},"4":{"en":"Ganti Mohana Chandra Balayogi Indoor Stadium, Hyderabad","hi":"गंटी मोहन चंद्र बालयोगी इंडोर स्टेडियम, हैदराबाद"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Indira Gandhi Arena, New Delhi</b><br>The <b>India Open Super 750</b> badminton tournament held from <b>13-18 January 2026</b> was played at the <b>Indira Gandhi Arena</b> in <b>New Delhi</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>India Open</b> is part of the <b>BWF World Tour</b> and is graded as a <b>Super 750</b> event, giving it high ranking points.<br>• It is organised by the <b>Badminton Association of India</b> and has been held since <b>1973</b>, with the <b>KD Jadhav Indoor Hall</b> also used in some editions.<br>• Indian shuttlers such as <b>Prakash Padukone, Saina Nehwal, P.V. Sindhu and the pair of Satwiksairaj Rankireddy and Chirag Shetty</b> have won the title.<br>• Other major BWF events are the <b>All England Open, Malaysia Open and Indonesia Open</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – इंदिरा गांधी एरीना, नई दिल्ली</b><br><b>13-18 जनवरी 2026</b> तक आयोजित <b>इंडिया ओपन सुपर 750</b> बैडमिंटन प्रतियोगिता <b>नई दिल्ली</b> के <b>इंदिरा गांधी एरीना</b> में खेली गई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>इंडिया ओपन</b> <b>BWF विश्व टूर</b> का भाग है और इसे <b>सुपर 750</b> श्रेणी में रखा गया है, जिससे इसे उच्च रैंकिंग अंक मिलते हैं।<br>• इसका आयोजन <b>भारतीय बैडमिंटन संघ</b> करता है और यह <b>1973</b> से हो रहा है; कुछ संस्करणों में <b>केडी जाधव इंडोर हॉल</b> का भी उपयोग हुआ।<br>• <b>प्रकाश पादुकोण, साइना नेहवाल, पी.वी. सिंधु तथा सात्विकसाईराज रंकीरेड्डी एवं चिराग शेट्टी</b> जैसे भारतीय खिलाड़ियों ने खिताब जीता है।<br>• अन्य प्रमुख BWF प्रतियोगिताएँ <b>ऑल इंग्लैंड ओपन, मलेशिया ओपन तथा इंडोनेशिया ओपन</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000072024","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"The India Open Super 750 badminton tournament, held from 13-18 January 2026, was hosted in which city? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"13-18 जनवरी 2026 तक आयोजित इंडिया ओपन सुपर 750 बैडमिंटन प्रतियोगिता किस नगर में आयोजित हुई? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"New Delhi","hi":"नई दिल्ली"},"2":{"en":"Hyderabad","hi":"हैदराबाद"},"3":{"en":"Bengaluru","hi":"बेंगलुरु"},"4":{"en":"Lucknow","hi":"लखनऊ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – New Delhi</b><br>The <b>India Open Super 750</b> badminton tournament held from <b>13-18 January 2026</b> was hosted in <b>New Delhi</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The tournament is played at the <b>Indira Gandhi Arena</b> in the capital and is one of the oldest badminton events in Asia.<br>• The <b>India Open</b> is a <b>BWF World Tour Super 750</b> event, ranking below only the Super 1000 tournaments and the World Tour Finals.<br>• The city has hosted major sporting events such as the <b>2010 Commonwealth Games</b>, the <b>2010 Hockey World Cup</b> and several <b>BWF India Open</b> editions.<br>• <b>Hyderabad</b>, <b>Bengaluru</b> and <b>Lucknow</b> have hosted other national and international badminton events.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – नई दिल्ली</b><br><b>13-18 जनवरी 2026</b> तक आयोजित <b>इंडिया ओपन सुपर 750</b> बैडमिंटन प्रतियोगिता <b>नई दिल्ली</b> में आयोजित हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह प्रतियोगिता राजधानी के <b>इंदिरा गांधी एरीना</b> में खेली जाती है और एशिया की सबसे पुरानी बैडमिंटन प्रतियोगिताओं में से एक है।<br>• <b>इंडिया ओपन</b> <b>BWF विश्व टूर सुपर 750</b> श्रेणी का आयोजन है, जो केवल सुपर 1000 तथा विश्व टूर फाइनल्स से नीचे है।<br>• इस नगर ने <b>2010 राष्ट्रमंडल खेल</b>, <b>2010 हॉकी विश्व कप</b> तथा कई <b>BWF इंडिया ओपन</b> संस्करणों जैसे प्रमुख खेल आयोजनों की मेजबानी की है।<br>• <b>हैदराबाद</b>, <b>बेंगलुरु</b> तथा <b>लखनऊ</b> ने अन्य राष्ट्रीय एवं अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बैडमिंटन आयोजनों की मेजबानी की है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000072025","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Politically administered prices were replaced under which economic reform strategy? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"राजनीतिक रूप से प्रशासित मूल्य किस आर्थिक सुधार रणनीति के अंतर्गत प्रतिस्थापित किए गए? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Cooperative pricing","hi":"सहकारी मूल्य निर्धारण"},"2":{"en":"Dual pricing","hi":"द्वि-मूल्य निर्धारण"},"3":{"en":"Public pricing","hi":"सार्वजनिक मूल्य निर्धारण"},"4":{"en":"Market determined pricing","hi":"बाजार निर्धारित मूल्य निर्धारण"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Market determined pricing</b><br>The 1991 reforms replaced <b>politically administered prices</b> with <b>market-determined prices</b>, allowing demand and supply to set prices in most sectors.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Administered prices were earlier fixed by the government for many industrial products, and the reforms <b>dereserved and decontrolled</b> large parts of industry.<br>• The reforms also removed <b>price controls under the Essential Commodities Act</b> for many items and reduced the ambit of <b>MRTP</b> restrictions.<br>• <b>Dual pricing</b> existed in the sugar and fertiliser sectors, where part of the output was sold at government-fixed rates and part in the open market.<br>• Even today, some prices remain administered, such as <b>minimum support prices for crops, LPG and some medicines</b> under the National Pharmaceutical Pricing Authority.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – बाजार निर्धारित मूल्य निर्धारण</b><br>1991 के सुधारों ने <b>राजनीतिक रूप से प्रशासित मूल्यों</b> को <b>बाजार-निर्धारित मूल्यों</b> से प्रतिस्थापित किया, जिससे अधिकांश क्षेत्रों में माँग तथा आपूर्ति मूल्य तय करने लगीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पहले अनेक औद्योगिक उत्पादों के मूल्य सरकार तय करती थी, तथा सुधारों ने उद्योग के बड़े भाग को <b>आरक्षण एवं नियंत्रण मुक्त</b> किया।<br>• सुधारों ने अनेक वस्तुओं के लिए <b>आवश्यक वस्तु अधिनियम</b> के अंतर्गत मूल्य नियंत्रण हटाए तथा <b>एमआरटीपी</b> प्रतिबंधों का दायरा घटाया।<br>• <b>द्वि-मूल्य निर्धारण</b> चीनी तथा उर्वरक क्षेत्र में था, जहाँ उत्पादन का भाग सरकारी दर पर और भाग खुले बाजार में बेचा जाता था।<br>• आज भी कुछ मूल्य प्रशासित हैं, जैसे <b>फसलों के न्यूनतम समर्थन मूल्य, एलपीजी तथा राष्ट्रीय औषधि मूल्य निर्धारण प्राधिकरण के अंतर्गत कुछ औषधियाँ</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000072026","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"India's Ease of Doing Business reform agenda primarily emphasizes which of the following? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत का व्यापार सुगमता सुधार एजेंडा मुख्यतः निम्नलिखित में से किस पर बल देता है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The use of manual procedures for granting business approvals.","hi":"व्यावसायिक स्वीकृतियों हेतु मैनुअल प्रक्रियाओं का उपयोग।"},"2":{"en":"The use of centralized physical offices for issuing business licences.","hi":"व्यावसायिक लाइसेंस जारी करने हेतु केंद्रीकृत भौतिक कार्यालयों का उपयोग।"},"3":{"en":"The digitization and online delivery of business related regulatory services.","hi":"व्यावसायिक नियामक सेवाओं का डिजिटलीकरण तथा ऑनलाइन वितरण।"},"4":{"en":"The use of physical documentation for completing business compliance procedures.","hi":"व्यावसायिक अनुपालन प्रक्रियाओं हेतु भौतिक दस्तावेज़ों का उपयोग।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The digitization and online delivery of business related regulatory services</b><br>India's <b>Ease of Doing Business</b> agenda emphasises the <b>digitisation and online delivery</b> of regulatory services, so approvals, licences and returns can be handled without physical visits.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Key measures include the <b>National Single Window System, online registration of companies and GST, digital signatures and e-filing</b>.<br>• The reforms seek to reduce <b>time, cost and the number of procedures</b> for starting and running a business.<br>• They are driven by the <b>DPIIT</b> through the <b>Business Reforms Action Plan</b> and are assessed on parameters such as <b>construction permits, utility connections and contract enforcement</b>.<br>• The approach also includes <b>decriminalisation of minor offences</b> and <b>risk-based inspections</b> to reduce the compliance burden.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – व्यावसायिक नियामक सेवाओं का डिजिटलीकरण तथा ऑनलाइन वितरण।</b><br>भारत का <b>व्यापार सुगमता</b> एजेंडा नियामक सेवाओं के <b>डिजिटलीकरण तथा ऑनलाइन वितरण</b> पर बल देता है, जिससे स्वीकृति, लाइसेंस तथा विवरणियाँ बिना भौतिक उपस्थिति के पूरी हो सकें।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रमुख उपायों में <b>राष्ट्रीय एकल खिड़की प्रणाली, कंपनियों का ऑनलाइन पंजीकरण, जीएसटी, डिजिटल हस्ताक्षर तथा ई-फाइलिंग</b> शामिल हैं।<br>• सुधारों का उद्देश्य व्यापार आरंभ करने तथा चलाने में लगने वाले <b>समय, लागत तथा प्रक्रियाओं की संख्या</b> घटाना है।<br>• इन्हें <b>DPIIT</b> <b>व्यापार सुधार कार्य योजना</b> के माध्यम से आगे बढ़ाता है और <b>निर्माण अनुमति, उपयोगिता कनेक्शन तथा अनुबंध प्रवर्तन</b> जैसे मानकों पर आकलन होता है।<br>• इस दृष्टिकोण में अनुपालन बोझ घटाने हेतु <b>लघु अपराधों का अपराधीकरण हटाना</b> तथा <b>जोखिम आधारित निरीक्षण</b> भी शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000072027","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A fixed amount of an ideal gas expands at constant pressure. If its volume becomes three times its initial volume, what will be its final absolute temperature in comparison with its initial absolute temperature? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित मात्रा की आदर्श गैस स्थिर दाब पर प्रसारित होती है। यदि उसका आयतन प्रारंभिक आयतन का तीन गुना हो जाए, तो उसका अंतिम परम तापमान प्रारंभिक परम तापमान की तुलना में क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It remains the same","hi":"यह समान रहता है"},"2":{"en":"It becomes twice the initial temperature","hi":"यह प्रारंभिक तापमान का दोगुना हो जाता है"},"3":{"en":"It becomes three times the initial temperature","hi":"यह प्रारंभिक तापमान का तीन गुना हो जाता है"},"4":{"en":"It becomes nine times the initial temperature","hi":"यह प्रारंभिक तापमान का नौ गुना हो जाता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – It becomes three times the initial temperature</b><br>By <b>Charles's law</b>, at constant pressure the volume of a fixed mass of gas is directly proportional to its absolute temperature, so if the volume triples, the <b>absolute temperature also triples</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The combined form of the gas laws gives <b>PV = nRT</b>, so at constant P and n, <b>V is proportional to T</b>.<br>• Absolute temperature must be taken in <b>kelvin</b>; using degrees Celsius in the formula gives wrong results.<br>• <b>Boyle's law</b> relates pressure and volume at constant temperature, and <b>Gay-Lussac's law</b> relates pressure and temperature at constant volume.<br>• In an isobaric process, the work done is <b>P times the change in volume</b>, and the heat supplied raises both internal energy and does external work.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – यह प्रारंभिक तापमान का तीन गुना हो जाता है</b><br><b>चार्ल्स के नियम</b> के अनुसार स्थिर दाब पर गैस की निश्चित मात्रा का आयतन उसके परम तापमान के समानुपाती होता है, अतः आयतन तीन गुना होने पर <b>परम तापमान भी तीन गुना</b> हो जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गैस नियमों का संयुक्त रूप <b>PV = nRT</b> देता है, अतः स्थिर P तथा n पर <b>V, T के समानुपाती</b> होता है।<br>• परम तापमान <b>केल्विन</b> में लिया जाना चाहिए; सेल्सियस में गणना करने पर गलत परिणाम मिलते हैं।<br>• <b>बॉयल का नियम</b> स्थिर ताप पर दाब तथा आयतन का संबंध देता है, तथा <b>गे-लुसाक का नियम</b> स्थिर आयतन पर दाब एवं ताप का।<br>• समदाबी प्रक्रिया में किया गया कार्य <b>P गुणा आयतन परिवर्तन</b> होता है, तथा दी गई ऊष्मा आंतरिक ऊर्जा बढ़ाने के साथ बाह्य कार्य भी करती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000072028","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Which statement best explains how biodiversity contributes to food security? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सा कथन सर्वोत्तम रूप से बताता है कि जैव विविधता खाद्य सुरक्षा में किस प्रकार योगदान करती है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Food security depends only on increasing fertilizer use.","hi":"खाद्य सुरक्षा केवल उर्वरक उपयोग बढ़ाने पर निर्भर है।"},"2":{"en":"Conserving wild relatives of crops is essential for future agricultural resilience.","hi":"फसलों के वन्य संबंधियों का संरक्षण भविष्य की कृषि सहनशीलता के लिए आवश्यक है।"},"3":{"en":"Genetic diversity decreases agricultural adaptability.","hi":"आनुवंशिक विविधता कृषि अनुकूलनशीलता घटाती है।"},"4":{"en":"Protected areas have no role in food security.","hi":"संरक्षित क्षेत्रों की खाद्य सुरक्षा में कोई भूमिका नहीं है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Conserving wild relatives of crops is essential for future agricultural resilience.</b><br><b>Wild relatives</b> of crops carry genes for <b>disease resistance, drought tolerance and higher yield</b>, so conserving them is essential for <b>future agricultural resilience and food security</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Genetic diversity</b> allows plant breeders to develop varieties that can withstand pests, diseases and climate stress.<br>• <b>Pollinators, soil micro-organisms and natural predators</b> of pests are part of biodiversity that directly supports crop production.<br>• <b>Protected areas and sacred groves</b> conserve wild relatives and ecosystem services, so they do contribute to food security.<br>• The <b>International Treaty on Plant Genetic Resources for Food and Agriculture</b> and the <b>Svalbard Global Seed Vault</b> aim to preserve this diversity.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – फसलों के वन्य संबंधियों का संरक्षण भविष्य की कृषि सहनशीलता के लिए आवश्यक है।</b><br>फसलों के <b>वन्य संबंधी</b> <b>रोग प्रतिरोध, सूखा सहनशीलता तथा अधिक उपज</b> के जीन रखते हैं, अतः उनका संरक्षण <b>भविष्य की कृषि सहनशीलता तथा खाद्य सुरक्षा</b> के लिए आवश्यक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>आनुवंशिक विविधता</b> से पादप प्रजनक ऐसी किस्में विकसित कर सकते हैं जो कीटों, रोगों तथा जलवायु तनाव को सह सकें।<br>• <b>परागणकर्ता, मृदा सूक्ष्मजीव तथा कीटों के प्राकृतिक शत्रु</b> जैव विविधता का वह भाग हैं जो सीधे फसल उत्पादन को सहारा देते हैं।<br>• <b>संरक्षित क्षेत्र तथा पवित्र उपवन</b> वन्य संबंधियों एवं पारितंत्र सेवाओं का संरक्षण करते हैं, अतः वे खाद्य सुरक्षा में योगदान देते हैं।<br>• <b>खाद्य एवं कृषि हेतु पादप आनुवंशिक संसाधनों पर अंतर्राष्ट्रीय संधि</b> तथा <b>स्वालबार्ड वैश्विक बीज भंडार</b> इस विविधता को सुरक्षित रखने का लक्ष्य रखते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000072029","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Forest and Grassland","question":{"en":"In a tropical evergreen forest, vegetation on the forest floor is generally sparse mainly because: [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उष्णकटिबंधीय सदाबहार वन में वन तल की वनस्पति सामान्यतः विरल होती है, मुख्यतः क्योंकि: [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The soil lacks nutrients due to heavy rainfall.","hi":"अधिक वर्षा के कारण मृदा में पोषक तत्वों की कमी होती है।"},"2":{"en":"Herbivores consume most ground vegetation.","hi":"शाकाहारी जीव अधिकांश भू-वनस्पति खा जाते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Dense canopy blocks sunlight.","hi":"घना छत्रक प्रकाश को रोक देता है।"},"4":{"en":"High humidity inhibits seed germination.","hi":"अधिक आर्द्रता बीज अंकुरण को रोकती है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Dense canopy blocks sunlight</b><br>In <b>tropical evergreen forests</b> the tall trees form a dense multi-layered <b>canopy</b> that blocks most <b>sunlight</b> from reaching the forest floor, so ground vegetation remains sparse.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• These forests occur in regions of <b>high rainfall (over 200 cm) and high temperature</b>, such as the Western Ghats, north-east India and the Andaman and Nicobar Islands.<br>• Species show <b>stratification</b>, with <b>emergent trees, a closed canopy, understory and shrub layers</b>, and most plants are <b>evergreen</b> with hard, waxy leaves.<br>• Litter decomposes rapidly in the <b>hot humid climate</b>, so nutrients are stored mainly in the <b>vegetation</b> rather than the soil.<br>• Other Indian forest types are <b>tropical deciduous, thorn, montane and mangrove</b> forests, each adapted to different rainfall and temperature conditions.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – घना छत्रक प्रकाश को रोक देता है।</b><br><b>उष्णकटिबंधीय सदाबहार वनों</b> में ऊँचे वृक्ष बहुस्तरीय घना <b>छत्रक</b> बनाते हैं जो वन तल तक पहुँचने वाले अधिकांश <b>प्रकाश</b> को रोक देता है, अतः भू-वनस्पति विरल रहती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ये वन <b>अधिक वर्षा (200 सेमी से अधिक) तथा उच्च तापमान</b> वाले क्षेत्रों में होते हैं, जैसे पश्चिमी घाट, पूर्वोत्तर भारत तथा अंडमान-निकोबार द्वीप।<br>• इनमें <b>स्तरीकरण</b> दिखता है - <b>बाहर निकले वृक्ष, बंद छत्रक, अधस्तर तथा झाड़ी स्तर</b> - और अधिकांश पौधे <b>सदाबहार</b> तथा कठोर मोमी पत्तियों वाले होते हैं।<br>• <b>गर्म आर्द्र जलवायु</b> में पर्णपात शीघ्र विघटित होता है, अतः पोषक तत्व मुख्यतः <b>वनस्पति</b> में संचित रहते हैं, मृदा में नहीं।<br>• भारत के अन्य वन प्रकार <b>उष्णकटिबंधीय पर्णपाती, कंटीले, पर्वतीय तथा मैंग्रोव</b> वन हैं, जो भिन्न वर्षा एवं तापमान के अनुकूल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000072030","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Microeconomics","question":{"en":"Which of the following would cause a movement along a supply curve rather than a shift in the supply curve? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा आपूर्ति वक्र के स्थानांतरण के बजाय आपूर्ति वक्र पर गति का कारण बनेगा? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"An improvement in production technology","hi":"उत्पादन तकनीक में सुधार"},"2":{"en":"An increase in the number of producers","hi":"उत्पादकों की संख्या में वृद्धि"},"3":{"en":"An increase in the commodity's own price","hi":"वस्तु के स्वयं के मूल्य में वृद्धि"},"4":{"en":"An increase in input prices","hi":"साधन मूल्यों में वृद्धि"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – An increase in the commodity's own price</b><br>A change in the <b>price of the commodity itself</b> causes <b>movement along the supply curve</b> (expansion or contraction of supply), not a shift.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A <b>shift of the supply curve</b> is caused by factors other than own price, such as <b>technology, input prices, number of sellers, taxes and subsidies and expectations</b>.<br>• <b>Expansion of supply</b> occurs when price rises and quantity supplied increases along the curve, while <b>contraction</b> occurs when price falls.<br>• Better technology and more producers shift the supply curve to the <b>right</b>, while higher input prices shift it to the <b>left</b>.<br>• The supply curve slopes <b>upward</b> in most markets because higher prices make production more profitable.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – वस्तु के स्वयं के मूल्य में वृद्धि</b><br><b>वस्तु के स्वयं के मूल्य</b> में परिवर्तन <b>आपूर्ति वक्र पर गति</b> (आपूर्ति का विस्तार अथवा संकुचन) उत्पन्न करता है, वक्र का स्थानांतरण नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>आपूर्ति वक्र का स्थानांतरण</b> स्वयं मूल्य के अतिरिक्त कारकों से होता है, जैसे <b>तकनीक, साधन मूल्य, विक्रेताओं की संख्या, कर एवं सब्सिडी तथा अपेक्षाएँ</b>।<br>• मूल्य बढ़ने पर आपूर्ति मात्रा बढ़ने से <b>आपूर्ति का विस्तार</b> होता है, तथा मूल्य घटने पर <b>संकुचन</b>।<br>• बेहतर तकनीक तथा अधिक उत्पादक आपूर्ति वक्र को <b>दाईं ओर</b> खिसकाते हैं, जबकि साधन मूल्य बढ़ने पर वक्र <b>बाईं ओर</b> खिसकता है।<br>• अधिकांश बाजारों में आपूर्ति वक्र <b>ऊपर की ओर</b> ढलान वाला होता है, क्योंकि अधिक मूल्य पर उत्पादन अधिक लाभदायक होता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000072031","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Examine the frequency polygon below to answer the following question.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/0197f407-29e1-7700-ad0a-dfc7e08ed730_EN.jpg?edu=639294382051319832\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>What is the total number of students represented in this data?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/0197f407-29e1-7700-ad0a-dfc7e08ed730_EN.jpg?edu=639294382051319832\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर देने के लिए नीचे दिए गए बारंबारता बहुभुज को देखिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/0197f407-29e1-7700-ad0a-dfc7e08ed730_HI.jpg?edu=639294382176194857\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>इस आँकड़े में दर्शाए गए विद्यार्थियों की कुल संख्या क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/0197f407-29e1-7700-ad0a-dfc7e08ed730_HI.jpg?edu=639294382176194857\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"78"},"2":{"en":"80"},"3":{"en":"75"},"4":{"en":"88"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Reading the polygon: 0–2 → 10, 2–4 → 22, 4–6 → 18, 6–8 → 15, 8–10 → 8, 10–12 → 5<br>Total \\(= 10 + 22 + 18 + 15 + 8 + 5\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{78}\\) students<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 78.</b>","hi":"बहुभुज से पढ़ने पर: 0–2 → 10, 2–4 → 22, 4–6 → 18, 6–8 → 15, 8–10 → 8, 10–12 → 5<br>कुल \\(= 10 + 22 + 18 + 15 + 8 + 5\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{78}\\) विद्यार्थी<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 78 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/0197f407-29e1-7700-ad0a-dfc7e08ed730_EN.jpg?edu=639294382051319832","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/0197f407-29e1-7700-ad0a-dfc7e08ed730_HI.jpg?edu=639294382176194857"]}},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000072032","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"A man travels to his destination at 60% of his normal walking speed and arrives 1 hour 40 minutes later than usual. Find his normal time (in hours) taken to reach the destination. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति अपनी सामान्य चाल के 60% से अपने गंतव्य तक जाता है और सामान्य समय से 1 घंटा 40 मिनट देरी से पहुँचता है। गंतव्य तक पहुँचने में उसका सामान्य समय (घंटों में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2.5 hours","hi":"2.5 घंटे"},"2":{"en":"3.5 hours","hi":"3.5 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"4.5 hours","hi":"4.5 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"5.5 hours","hi":"5.5 घंटे"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"At 60% of the speed, the time taken becomes \\(\\frac{T}{0.6} = \\frac{5T}{3}\\)<br>Extra time \\(= \\frac{5T}{3} - T = \\frac{2T}{3} = 1\\frac{2}{3}\\) hours<br>\\(T = \\frac{5}{3} \\times \\frac{3}{2} = \\boxed{2.5}\\) hours<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2.5 hours.</b>","hi":"चाल 60% होने पर लगने वाला समय \\(\\frac{T}{0.6} = \\frac{5T}{3}\\)<br>अतिरिक्त समय \\(= \\frac{5T}{3} - T = \\frac{2T}{3} = 1\\frac{2}{3}\\) घंटे<br>\\(T = \\frac{5}{3} \\times \\frac{3}{2} = \\boxed{2.5}\\) घंटे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2.5 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000072033","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If 0.13 ÷ p = 13, what is the value of p? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 0.13 ÷ p = 13 है, तो p का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.25"},"2":{"en":"0.01"},"3":{"en":"1.78"},"4":{"en":"0.05"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(p = \\frac{0.13}{13}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{13}{1300} = \\boxed{0.01}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.01.</b>","hi":"\\(p = \\frac{0.13}{13}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{13}{1300} = \\boxed{0.01}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0.01 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000072034","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Evaluate: \\(\\frac{0.001-0.008}{0.01+0.02+0.04}\\). [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: \\(\\frac{0.001-0.008}{0.01+0.02+0.04}\\) [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.2"},"2":{"en":"−0.1"},"3":{"en":"−0.3"},"4":{"en":"0.4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Numerator \\(= 0.001 - 0.008 = -0.007\\)<br>Denominator \\(= 0.01 + 0.02 + 0.04 = 0.07\\)<br>Value \\(= \\frac{-0.007}{0.07} = \\boxed{-0.1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): −0.1.</b>","hi":"अंश \\(= 0.001 - 0.008 = -0.007\\)<br>हर \\(= 0.01 + 0.02 + 0.04 = 0.07\\)<br>मान \\(= \\frac{-0.007}{0.07} = \\boxed{-0.1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): −0.1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000072035","section":"MATH","topic":"LCM and HCF","question":{"en":"Determine the number of integers between 1 and 500 that are divisible by 3, 4, and 5. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1 और 500 के बीच उन पूर्णांकों की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए जो 3, 4 और 5 से विभाज्य हैं। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"9"},"4":{"en":"10"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Divisible by 3, 4 and 5 means divisible by LCM(3, 4, 5) = 60<br>Multiples of 60 up to 500: 60, 120, …, 480<br>Number \\(= \\left\\lfloor\\frac{500}{60}\\right\\rfloor = 8\\)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 8.</b>","hi":"3, 4 और 5 से विभाज्यता का अर्थ है LCM(3, 4, 5) = 60 से विभाज्यता<br>500 तक 60 के गुणज: 60, 120, …, 480<br>संख्या \\(= \\left\\lfloor\\frac{500}{60}\\right\\rfloor = 8\\)<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000072036","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"In a partnership, A invests ₹4,000 for the whole year. B starts at ₹6,000 and increases to ₹8,000 after 4 months. C joins after 9 months with ₹10,000. What is the ratio by which the annual profit should be divided? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक साझेदारी में A पूरे वर्ष के लिए ₹4,000 निवेश करता है। B, ₹6,000 से प्रारंभ करता है और 4 महीने बाद इसे ₹8,000 कर देता है। C, 9 महीने बाद ₹10,000 के साथ शामिल होता है। वार्षिक लाभ किस अनुपात में विभाजित होना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 : 19 : 15"},"2":{"en":"24 : 44 : 15"},"3":{"en":"12 : 22 : 15"},"4":{"en":"24 : 38 : 15"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A: \\(4000 \\times 12 = 48{,}000\\)<br>B: \\(6000 \\times 4 + 8000 \\times 8 = 24{,}000 + 64{,}000 = 88{,}000\\)<br>C: \\(10{,}000 \\times 3 = 30{,}000\\)<br>Ratio \\(= 48 : 88 : 30 = \\boxed{24 : 44 : 15}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 24 : 44 : 15.</b>","hi":"A: \\(4000 \\times 12 = 48{,}000\\)<br>B: \\(6000 \\times 4 + 8000 \\times 8 = 24{,}000 + 64{,}000 = 88{,}000\\)<br>C: \\(10{,}000 \\times 3 = 30{,}000\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= 48 : 88 : 30 = \\boxed{24 : 44 : 15}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 24 : 44 : 15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000072037","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"Given that the average of four consecutive even numbers is 15, determine the second largest number in the sequence. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि चार क्रमागत सम संख्याओं का औसत 15 है, तो उस क्रम में दूसरी सबसे बड़ी संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12"},"2":{"en":"16"},"3":{"en":"14"},"4":{"en":"18"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the numbers be \\(n, n+2, n+4, n+6\\). Average \\(= n + 3 = 15 \\Rightarrow n = 12\\)<br>The numbers are 12, 14, 16, 18<br>Second largest \\(= \\boxed{16}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 16.</b>","hi":"संख्याएँ \\(n, n+2, n+4, n+6\\) मानिए। औसत \\(= n + 3 = 15 \\Rightarrow n = 12\\)<br>संख्याएँ 12, 14, 16, 18 हैं<br>दूसरी सबसे बड़ी \\(= \\boxed{16}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 16 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000072038","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"If the lines represented by x + y = 1, x − y = 5, and 3x + 4y = k are concurrent (passing through the same point), find the value of (k + 5). [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि x + y = 1, x − y = 5 और 3x + 4y = k द्वारा निरूपित रेखाएँ संगामी हैं (एक ही बिंदु से गुज़रती हैं), तो (k + 5) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"0"},"4":{"en":"7"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Solving \\(x + y = 1\\) and \\(x - y = 5\\): adding gives \\(2x = 6 \\Rightarrow x = 3\\), so \\(y = -2\\)<br>Point of concurrence = (3, −2)<br>\\(k = 3(3) + 4(-2) = 9 - 8 = 1\\)<br>\\(k + 5 = \\boxed{6}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 6.</b>","hi":"\\(x + y = 1\\) और \\(x - y = 5\\) हल करने पर: जोड़ने से \\(2x = 6 \\Rightarrow x = 3\\), अतः \\(y = -2\\)<br>संगम बिंदु = (3, −2)<br>\\(k = 3(3) + 4(-2) = 9 - 8 = 1\\)<br>\\(k + 5 = \\boxed{6}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 6 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000072039","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A hollow cuboid has a length of 25 cm, a breadth of 20 cm, and a height of 15 cm, with a wall thickness of 2 cm. Find the volume of the solid material. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक खोखले घनाभ की लंबाई 25 cm, चौड़ाई 20 cm और ऊँचाई 15 cm है, तथा दीवार की मोटाई 2 cm है। ठोस पदार्थ का आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4312 cm³"},"2":{"en":"3170 cm³"},"3":{"en":"3804 cm³"},"4":{"en":"4978 cm³"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Outer volume \\(= 25 \\times 20 \\times 15 = 7500\\) cm³<br>Inner dimensions \\(= (25-4) \\times (20-4) \\times (15-4) = 21 \\times 16 \\times 11 = 3696\\) cm³<br>Solid material \\(= 7500 - 3696\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3804}\\) cm³<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3804 cm³.</b>","hi":"बाहरी आयतन \\(= 25 \\times 20 \\times 15 = 7500\\) cm³<br>भीतरी विमाएँ \\(= (25-4) \\times (20-4) \\times (15-4) = 21 \\times 16 \\times 11 = 3696\\) cm³<br>ठोस पदार्थ \\(= 7500 - 3696\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3804}\\) cm³<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3804 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000072040","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"A wheel rotates at 50π radians per second. How many revolutions does it make in one minute? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक पहिया 50π रेडियन प्रति सेकंड की दर से घूमता है। यह एक मिनट में कितने चक्कर लगाएगा? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1200"},"2":{"en":"1900"},"3":{"en":"1500"},"4":{"en":"1800"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Revolutions per second \\(= \\frac{50\\pi}{2\\pi} = 25\\)<br>Revolutions per minute \\(= 25 \\times 60\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1500}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1500.</b>","hi":"प्रति सेकंड चक्कर \\(= \\frac{50\\pi}{2\\pi} = 25\\)<br>प्रति मिनट चक्कर \\(= 25 \\times 60\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1500}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1500 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000072041","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If secθ = 17/15 and θ is an acute angle, find 2(cosecθ − cotθ). [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि secθ = 17/15 है और θ एक न्यून कोण है, तो 2(cosecθ − cotθ) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{15}{17}\\), so \\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{8}{17}\\)<br>\\(\\csc\\theta - \\cot\\theta = \\frac{17}{8} - \\frac{15}{8} = \\frac{2}{8} = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(2(\\csc\\theta - \\cot\\theta) = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{15}{17}\\), अतः \\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{8}{17}\\)<br>\\(\\csc\\theta - \\cot\\theta = \\frac{17}{8} - \\frac{15}{8} = \\frac{2}{8} = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(2(\\csc\\theta - \\cot\\theta) = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000072042","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\sqrt{7 - 4\\sqrt{3}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7 - 4\\sqrt{3}}}\\). [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{7 - 4\\sqrt{3}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7 - 4\\sqrt{3}}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(-2\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"−4"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(7 - 4\\sqrt{3} = (2 - \\sqrt{3})^2\\), so \\(\\sqrt{7 - 4\\sqrt{3}} = 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{2 - \\sqrt{3}} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>Value \\(= (2 - \\sqrt{3}) - (2 + \\sqrt{3}) = \\boxed{-2\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(-2\\sqrt{3}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(7 - 4\\sqrt{3} = (2 - \\sqrt{3})^2\\), अतः \\(\\sqrt{7 - 4\\sqrt{3}} = 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{2 - \\sqrt{3}} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>मान \\(= (2 - \\sqrt{3}) - (2 + \\sqrt{3}) = \\boxed{-2\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(-2\\sqrt{3}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000072043","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The following pie-chart shows the percentage distribution of energy consumption from various sources. Study the pie-chart carefully and answer the question based on it.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e6d95-ebae-7798-a759-50c6061502fa_EN.jpg?edu=639294382052708505\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>If the government mandates a transition where 50% of the 'Coal' consumption is replaced by 'Solar & Wind', what will be the new percentage share of 'Solar & Wind' in the total energy mix?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e6d95-ebae-7798-a759-50c6061502fa_EN.jpg?edu=639294382052708505\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित पाई-चार्ट विभिन्न स्रोतों से ऊर्जा खपत का प्रतिशत वितरण दर्शाता है। पाई-चार्ट को ध्यानपूर्वक पढ़िए और उसके आधार पर प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019e6d95-ebae-7798-a759-50c6061502fa_HI.jpg?edu=639294382177264144\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>यदि सरकार एक ऐसा परिवर्तन अनिवार्य करती है जिसमें 'कोयला' खपत का 50% 'सौर और पवन' से प्रतिस्थापित हो जाता है, तो कुल ऊर्जा मिश्रण में 'सौर और पवन' का नया प्रतिशत हिस्सा क्या होगा?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019e6d95-ebae-7798-a759-50c6061502fa_HI.jpg?edu=639294382177264144\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25%"},"2":{"en":"35%"},"3":{"en":"20%"},"4":{"en":"30%"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"From the pie chart: Coal 30%, Natural Gas 20%, Petroleum 20%, Hydroelectric 15%, Solar & Wind 15%<br>Coal transferred \\(= 50\\%\\) of \\(30\\% = 15\\%\\)<br>New Solar & Wind share \\(= 15\\% + 15\\% = \\boxed{30\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 30%.</b>","hi":"पाई चार्ट से: कोयला 30%, प्राकृतिक गैस 20%, पेट्रोलियम 20%, जलविद्युत 15%, सौर और पवन 15%<br>हस्तांतरित कोयला \\(= 30\\%\\) का \\(50\\% = 15\\%\\)<br>सौर और पवन का नया हिस्सा \\(= 15\\% + 15\\% = \\boxed{30\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 30% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019e6d95-ebae-7798-a759-50c6061502fa_EN.jpg?edu=639294382052708505","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019e6d95-ebae-7798-a759-50c6061502fa_HI.jpg?edu=639294382177264144"]}},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000072044","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If 2sinθ − 1 = 0, what is the value of the acute angle θ? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 2sinθ − 1 = 0 है, तो न्यून कोण θ का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30°"},"2":{"en":"45°"},"3":{"en":"60°"},"4":{"en":"90°"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(2\\sin\\theta = 1 \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>For an acute angle, \\(\\theta = \\boxed{30^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 30°.</b>","hi":"\\(2\\sin\\theta = 1 \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>न्यून कोण के लिए, \\(\\theta = \\boxed{30^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 30° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000072045","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"Machine A and Machine B working together can print a batch of books in 12 hours. If Machine A works at half of its normal speed and Machine B operates at three times its normal speed, both together complete the same work in 8 hours. How long would it take Machine A, working at its normal speed alone, to print the entire batch? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मशीन A और मशीन B मिलकर पुस्तकों का एक बैच 12 घंटे में प्रिंट कर सकती हैं। यदि मशीन A अपनी सामान्य चाल के आधे भाग पर कार्य करे और मशीन B अपनी सामान्य चाल के तीन गुना पर कार्य करे, तो दोनों मिलकर वही कार्य 8 घंटे में पूरा करती हैं। मशीन A अकेली अपनी सामान्य चाल से पूरा बैच कितने समय में प्रिंट करेगी? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 hrs","hi":"20 घंटे"},"2":{"en":"18 hrs","hi":"18 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"21 hrs","hi":"21 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"24 hrs","hi":"24 घंटे"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Let A's rate be \\(a\\) and B's rate be \\(b\\) per hour<br>\\(a + b = \\frac{1}{12}\\) and \\(\\frac{a}{2} + 3b = \\frac{1}{8}\\)<br>Substituting \\(b = \\frac{1}{12} - a\\): \\(\\frac{a}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} - 3a = \\frac{1}{8}\\)<br>\\(-\\frac{5a}{2} = \\frac{1}{8} - \\frac{1}{4} = -\\frac{1}{8} \\Rightarrow a = \\frac{1}{20}\\)<br>A alone takes \\(\\boxed{20}\\) hrs<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 20 hrs.</b>","hi":"A की दर \\(a\\) और B की दर \\(b\\) प्रति घंटा मानिए<br>\\(a + b = \\frac{1}{12}\\) और \\(\\frac{a}{2} + 3b = \\frac{1}{8}\\)<br>\\(b = \\frac{1}{12} - a\\) रखने पर: \\(\\frac{a}{2} + \\frac{1}{4} - 3a = \\frac{1}{8}\\)<br>\\(-\\frac{5a}{2} = \\frac{1}{8} - \\frac{1}{4} = -\\frac{1}{8} \\Rightarrow a = \\frac{1}{20}\\)<br>A अकेली \\(\\boxed{20}\\) घंटे लेती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 20 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000072046","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Evaluate: tan 30° tan 60° − sec 30° cosec 60° + sin² 30° + sin² 60° [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: tan 30° tan 60° − sec 30° cosec 60° + sin² 30° + sin² 60° [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4}{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{3}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan 30^\\circ\\tan 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\times \\sqrt{3} = 1\\)<br>\\(\\sec 30^\\circ\\csc 60^\\circ = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\times \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{4}{3}\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2 30^\\circ + \\sin^2 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = 1\\)<br>Expression \\(= 1 - \\frac{4}{3} + 1 = \\boxed{\\frac{2}{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan 30^\\circ\\tan 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\times \\sqrt{3} = 1\\)<br>\\(\\sec 30^\\circ\\csc 60^\\circ = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\times \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{4}{3}\\)<br>\\(\\sin^2 30^\\circ + \\sin^2 60^\\circ = \\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{3}{4} = 1\\)<br>व्यंजक \\(= 1 - \\frac{4}{3} + 1 = \\boxed{\\frac{2}{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000072047","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"What is the exact value of the expression (8.35)² − (1.45)²? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"व्यंजक (8.35)² − (1.45)² का सटीक मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"47.61"},"2":{"en":"63.92"},"3":{"en":"67.62"},"4":{"en":"71.83"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)\\)<br>\\(= (8.35 + 1.45)(8.35 - 1.45) = 9.80 \\times 6.90\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{67.62}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 67.62.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a + b)(a - b)\\)<br>\\(= (8.35 + 1.45)(8.35 - 1.45) = 9.80 \\times 6.90\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{67.62}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 67.62 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000072048","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In ΔABC, the interior angle bisectors of ∠B and ∠C intersect at point I. A line passing through I is parallel to BC and intersects the segments AB and AC at points P and Q respectively. If AB = 12 units and AC = 15 units, what is the perimeter of triangle APQ? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ΔABC में, ∠B और ∠C के अंतः कोण समद्विभाजक बिंदु I पर प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं। I से गुज़रने वाली एक रेखा BC के समांतर है और खंडों AB तथा AC को क्रमशः बिंदु P और Q पर प्रतिच्छेद करती है। यदि AB = 12 इकाई और AC = 15 इकाई है, तो त्रिभुज APQ का परिमाप क्या है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 units","hi":"20 इकाई"},"2":{"en":"22 units","hi":"22 इकाई"},"3":{"en":"24 units","hi":"24 इकाई"},"4":{"en":"27 units","hi":"27 इकाई"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Since PQ ∥ BC, \\(\\angle PIB = \\angle IBC = \\angle IBP\\), so \\(BP = PI\\)<br>Similarly \\(CQ = QI\\)<br>Perimeter of APQ \\(= AP + PQ + AQ = AP + PI + IQ + AQ\\)<br>\\(= AP + PB + CQ + AQ = AB + AC = 12 + 15\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{27}\\) units<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 27 units.</b>","hi":"PQ ∥ BC होने से, \\(\\angle PIB = \\angle IBC = \\angle IBP\\), अतः \\(BP = PI\\)<br>इसी प्रकार \\(CQ = QI\\)<br>APQ का परिमाप \\(= AP + PQ + AQ = AP + PI + IQ + AQ\\)<br>\\(= AP + PB + CQ + AQ = AB + AC = 12 + 15\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{27}\\) इकाई<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 27 इकाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000072049","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"If √a + √b = √c + √d, where a, b, c, and d are distinct prime numbers, which of the following statements must be true? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि √a + √b = √c + √d है, जहाँ a, b, c और d भिन्न अभाज्य संख्याएँ हैं, तो निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन अनिवार्यतः सत्य है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The primes a, b, c, and d must be in arithmetic progression.","hi":"अभाज्य संख्याएँ a, b, c और d समांतर श्रेणी में होनी चाहिए।"},"2":{"en":"a + b = c + d and ab = cd.","hi":"a + b = c + d और ab = cd."},"3":{"en":"No four distinct prime numbers can satisfy this equation.","hi":"कोई भी चार भिन्न अभाज्य संख्याएँ इस समीकरण को संतुष्ट नहीं कर सकतीं।"},"4":{"en":"Infinitely many combinations of such distinct primes exist.","hi":"ऐसी भिन्न अभाज्य संख्याओं के अपरिमित रूप से अनेक संयोजन मौजूद हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Squaring: \\(a + b + 2\\sqrt{ab} = c + d + 2\\sqrt{cd}\\)<br>The irrational parts must match, giving \\(ab = cd\\)<br>Since a, b are distinct primes, the pair {a, b} is the unique prime factorisation of ab; hence {c, d} = {a, b}, contradicting distinctness<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{\\text{No four distinct prime numbers can satisfy this equation.}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): No four distinct prime numbers can satisfy this equation..</b>","hi":"वर्ग करने पर: \\(a + b + 2\\sqrt{ab} = c + d + 2\\sqrt{cd}\\)<br>अपरिमेय भाग बराबर होने चाहिए, जिससे \\(ab = cd\\)<br>a, b भिन्न अभाज्य हैं, अतः ab का अभाज्य गुणनखंडन अद्वितीय है; इसलिए {c, d} = {a, b}, जो भिन्नता का विरोध करता है<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{\\text{कोई भी चार भिन्न अभाज्य संख्याएँ इस समीकरण को संतुष्ट नहीं कर सकतीं।}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): कोई भी चार भिन्न अभाज्य संख्याएँ इस समीकरण को संतुष्ट नहीं कर सकतीं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000072050","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"An alloy of zinc, copper, and tin contains 70% zinc and 20% copper by weight. A second alloy containing only zinc and tin is melted and mixed with the first alloy. The resulting mixture contains 56% zinc and 14% copper by weight. Find the percentage of zinc in the second alloy. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जिंक, तांबा और टिन के एक मिश्रातु में भार से 70% जिंक और 20% तांबा है। केवल जिंक और टिन वाला दूसरा मिश्रातु पिघलाकर पहले मिश्रातु के साथ मिलाया जाता है। परिणामी मिश्रण में भार से 56% जिंक और 14% तांबा है। दूसरे मिश्रातु में जिंक का प्रतिशत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"21.33%"},"2":{"en":"22.33%"},"3":{"en":"23.33%"},"4":{"en":"24.33%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Copper comes only from the first alloy. If a fraction \\(f\\) of the mixture is the first alloy:<br>\\(0.20f = 0.14 \\Rightarrow f = 0.7\\)<br>Zinc balance: \\(0.70(0.7) + x(0.3) = 0.56\\)<br>\\(0.49 + 0.3x = 0.56 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{0.07}{0.3} = 23.33\\%\\)<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{23.33\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 23.33%.</b>","hi":"तांबा केवल पहले मिश्रातु से आता है। यदि मिश्रण का \\(f\\) भाग पहला मिश्रातु है:<br>\\(0.20f = 0.14 \\Rightarrow f = 0.7\\)<br>जिंक का संतुलन: \\(0.70(0.7) + x(0.3) = 0.56\\)<br>\\(0.49 + 0.3x = 0.56 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{0.07}{0.3} = 23.33\\%\\)<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{23.33\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 23.33% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000072051","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two distinct coplanar circles touch each other internally. How many common tangents can be drawn to these two circles? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो भिन्न समतलीय वृत्त एक-दूसरे को आंतरिक रूप से स्पर्श करते हैं। इन दोनों वृत्तों पर कितनी उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ खींची जा सकती हैं? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"For circles touching internally, \\(d = R - r\\)<br>There is only one common tangent, namely the tangent at the point of contact<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"आंतरिक रूप से स्पर्श करने वाले वृत्तों के लिए \\(d = R - r\\)<br>केवल एक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा होती है, अर्थात् स्पर्श बिंदु पर स्पर्श रेखा<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000072052","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"A regional network operator measures the data recovery success speed of two distinct server nodes (Node A and Node B) across four testing scenarios. The findings are given in the following bar-graph:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019f890b-5a31-7d35-95b6-64f59aaa207b_EN.jpg?edu=639294382055141562\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>In how many scenarios did Node A outperform Node B by a margin equivalent to more than 15% of Node B's performance in that specific scenario?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019f890b-5a31-7d35-95b6-64f59aaa207b_EN.jpg?edu=639294382055141562\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक क्षेत्रीय नेटवर्क ऑपरेटर चार परीक्षण परिदृश्यों में दो भिन्न सर्वर नोड्स (नोड A और नोड B) की डेटा रिकवरी सफलता गति मापता है। निष्कर्ष निम्नलिखित स्तंभ ग्राफ में दिए गए हैं:<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f890b-5a31-7d35-95b6-64f59aaa207b_HI.jpg?edu=639294382179092955\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>कितने परिदृश्यों में नोड A ने नोड B को उस विशिष्ट परिदृश्य में नोड B के प्रदर्शन के 15% से अधिक के अंतर से पीछे छोड़ा?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f890b-5a31-7d35-95b6-64f59aaa207b_HI.jpg?edu=639294382179092955\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From the graph: Scenario 1 → A 40, B 35; Scenario 2 → A 55, B 60; Scenario 3 → A 30, B 45; Scenario 4 → A 65, B 50<br>Scenario 1: \\(\\frac{40 - 35}{35} = 14.3\\%\\) (not more than 15%)<br>Scenario 4: \\(\\frac{65 - 50}{50} = 30\\%\\) ✓<br>In scenarios 2 and 3, A is below B<br>Hence \\(\\boxed{1}\\) scenario<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"ग्राफ से: परिदृश्य 1 → A 40, B 35; परिदृश्य 2 → A 55, B 60; परिदृश्य 3 → A 30, B 45; परिदृश्य 4 → A 65, B 50<br>परिदृश्य 1: \\(\\frac{40 - 35}{35} = 14.3\\%\\) (15% से अधिक नहीं)<br>परिदृश्य 4: \\(\\frac{65 - 50}{50} = 30\\%\\) ✓<br>परिदृश्य 2 और 3 में A, B से कम है<br>इसलिए \\(\\boxed{1}\\) परिदृश्य<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/EN/019f890b-5a31-7d35-95b6-64f59aaa207b_EN.jpg?edu=639294382055141562","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct28/qimg/1/HI/019f890b-5a31-7d35-95b6-64f59aaa207b_HI.jpg?edu=639294382179092955"]}},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000072053","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"A total of ₹12,000 is divided between Scheme A and Scheme B. ₹P is invested in A at \\(12\\frac{1}{2}\\%\\) simple interest per annum for 3 years and ₹(12,000 − P) in B at 20% compound interest per annum for 2 years. If Scheme B earns ₹64 more interest than Scheme A, find P. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कुल ₹12,000 को योजना A और योजना B के बीच विभाजित किया जाता है। ₹P, योजना A में 3 वर्षों के लिए \\(12\\frac{1}{2}\\%\\) प्रति वर्ष साधारण ब्याज पर और ₹(12,000 − P), योजना B में 2 वर्षों के लिए 20% प्रति वर्ष चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर निवेश किए जाते हैं। यदि योजना B, योजना A से ₹64 अधिक ब्याज देती है, तो P ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹6,000"},"2":{"en":"₹6,400"},"3":{"en":"₹6,800"},"4":{"en":"₹7,200"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Interest from A \\(= P \\times \\frac{12.5}{100} \\times 3 = 0.375P\\)<br>Interest from B \\(= (12{,}000 - P)\\left[(1.2)^2 - 1\\right] = 0.44(12{,}000 - P)\\)<br>\\(0.44(12{,}000 - P) - 0.375P = 64\\)<br>\\(5280 - 0.815P = 64 \\Rightarrow 0.815P = 5216\\)<br>\\(P = \\boxed{6400}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹6,400.</b>","hi":"A से ब्याज \\(= P \\times \\frac{12.5}{100} \\times 3 = 0.375P\\)<br>B से ब्याज \\(= (12{,}000 - P)\\left[(1.2)^2 - 1\\right] = 0.44(12{,}000 - P)\\)<br>\\(0.44(12{,}000 - P) - 0.375P = 64\\)<br>\\(5280 - 0.815P = 64 \\Rightarrow 0.815P = 5216\\)<br>\\(P = \\boxed{6400}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹6,400 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000072054","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"The total wages paid to all technicians and all assistants are in the ratio 7 : 9, while the wage per technician and per assistant is in the ratio 5 : 6. If there are 203 employees altogether, how many are technicians? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सभी तकनीशियनों और सभी सहायकों को दिए गए कुल वेतन 7 : 9 के अनुपात में हैं, जबकि प्रति तकनीशियन और प्रति सहायक वेतन 5 : 6 के अनुपात में है। यदि कुल 203 कर्मचारी हैं, तो कितने तकनीशियन हैं? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"98"},"2":{"en":"91"},"3":{"en":"105"},"4":{"en":"112"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Number ratio = wage ratio ÷ per-person wage ratio<br>Technicians : assistants \\(= \\frac{7}{5} : \\frac{9}{6} = 42 : 45 = 14 : 15\\)<br>Total parts \\(= 29\\); \\(203 = 29 \\times 7\\)<br>Technicians \\(= 14 \\times 7 = \\boxed{98}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 98.</b>","hi":"संख्या अनुपात = वेतन अनुपात ÷ प्रति व्यक्ति वेतन अनुपात<br>तकनीशियन : सहायक \\(= \\frac{7}{5} : \\frac{9}{6} = 42 : 45 = 14 : 15\\)<br>कुल भाग \\(= 29\\); \\(203 = 29 \\times 7\\)<br>तकनीशियन \\(= 14 \\times 7 = \\boxed{98}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 98 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000072055","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A person divides ₹47,200 into three parts and invests all three at \\(6\\frac{1}{4}\\%\\) per annum simple interest for 4 years, 8 years and 16 years respectively. If the amounts received at the end of the respective periods are equal, what is the difference between the part invested for 4 years and the part invested for 16 years? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति ₹47,200 को तीन भागों में विभाजित करके तीनों को \\(6\\frac{1}{4}\\%\\) प्रति वर्ष साधारण ब्याज पर क्रमशः 4 वर्ष, 8 वर्ष और 16 वर्ष के लिए निवेश करता है। यदि संबंधित अवधियों के अंत में प्राप्त राशियाँ बराबर हैं, तो 4 वर्ष के लिए निवेश किए गए भाग और 16 वर्ष के लिए निवेश किए गए भाग का अंतर क्या है? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹6,400"},"2":{"en":"₹6,800"},"3":{"en":"₹7,000"},"4":{"en":"₹7,200"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Rate \\(= 6.25\\%\\), so multipliers are \\(1 + 0.0625t\\): for 4 years 1.25, for 8 years 1.5, for 16 years 2<br>If each final amount is A, the parts are \\(\\frac{A}{1.25}, \\frac{A}{1.5}, \\frac{A}{2}\\)<br>\\(A(0.8 + 0.6667 + 0.5) = 47200 \\Rightarrow A \\times \\frac{59}{30} = 47200 \\Rightarrow A = 24{,}000\\)<br>Parts: 19,200 and 12,000; difference \\(= \\boxed{7200}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹7,200.</b>","hi":"दर \\(= 6.25\\%\\), अतः गुणक \\(1 + 0.0625t\\) हैं: 4 वर्ष के लिए 1.25, 8 वर्ष के लिए 1.5, 16 वर्ष के लिए 2<br>यदि प्रत्येक अंतिम राशि A है, तो भाग \\(\\frac{A}{1.25}, \\frac{A}{1.5}, \\frac{A}{2}\\)<br>\\(A(0.8 + 0.6667 + 0.5) = 47200 \\Rightarrow A \\times \\frac{59}{30} = 47200 \\Rightarrow A = 24{,}000\\)<br>भाग: 19,200 और 12,000; अंतर \\(= \\boxed{7200}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹7,200 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000072056","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) at district headquarters<br>B) to streamline service delivery<br>C) citizen facilitation centres<br>D) have been established [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"D-C-B-A"},"2":{"en":"C-D-A-B"},"3":{"en":"C-A-D-B"},"4":{"en":"A-C-D-B"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: C-D-A-B</b><br>C and D form the subject and passive predicate.<br>A gives the location: district headquarters.<br>B states the purpose: streamlined service delivery.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): C-D-A-B.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000072057","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Identify the option that best corrects the highlighted part of the sentence for proper grammar and usage.<br>She is <b>more smarter</b> than her brother. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"smarter"},"2":{"en":"smartest"},"3":{"en":"extra smart"},"4":{"en":"more smartest"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Do not combine “more” with the comparative “smarter.”</b><br>Correct sentence: “She is <b>smarter</b> than her brother.”<br>“Smartest” is superlative, and “more smartest” is doubly marked.<br>“Extra smart” does not form the direct comparison.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): smarter.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000072058","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"What is the one-word substitute for:<br>“The pathological fear of open spaces or being in situations where escape might be difficult.” [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nyctophobia"},"2":{"en":"Nyctophobia"},"3":{"en":"Agoraphobia"},"4":{"en":"Xenophobia"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Agoraphobia (खुली जगह का भय) = fear of open or inescapable situations.</b><br><b>Nyctophobia</b> = fear of darkness<br><b>Xenophobia</b> = fear or hatred of foreigners<br>Only “agoraphobia” matches the definition.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Agoraphobia.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000072059","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"There are four jumbled sentences given below. Your task is to rearrange them into a logically coherent and meaningful paragraph and choose the correct sequence from the given options.<br>1. It blends entertainment, sports, and business.<br>2. The Indian Premier League (IPL) has transformed cricket into a festival.<br>3. The league generates massive viewership and revenues.<br>4. Players from around the world participate each season. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4-1-3-2"},"2":{"en":"1-3-2-4"},"3":{"en":"1-2-4-3"},"4":{"en":"2-1-4-3"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-1-4-3</b><br>Sentence 2 introduces the IPL’s transformation of cricket.<br>Sentence 1 explains its blend of fields, followed by international participation in 4.<br>Sentence 3 concludes with viewership and revenues.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2-1-4-3.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000072060","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"What is the antonym of the word “meticulous”? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Careless"},"2":{"en":"Detailed"},"3":{"en":"Flexible"},"4":{"en":"Precise"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Meticulous (सूक्ष्मता से काम करने वाला) = very careful.</b><br><b>Careless (लापरवाह)</b> = negligent ✔<br><b>Detailed (विस्तृत)</b> = thorough<br><b>Flexible (लचीला)</b> = adaptable; <b>precise (यथार्थ)</b> = exact.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Careless.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000072061","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Fly in the face of” [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Challenge or contradict"},"2":{"en":"Fly over someone's head"},"3":{"en":"Travel by flight"},"4":{"en":"Act suspiciously"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Fly in the face of (खुला विरोध करना) = openly contradict.</b><br>Example: “His actions fly in the face of established rules.”<br>Literal flying and suspicious behaviour are unrelated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Challenge or contradict.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000072062","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Face the music” [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Attend a concert"},"2":{"en":"Deal with consequences"},"3":{"en":"Celebrate"},"4":{"en":"Avoid issues"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Face the music (परिणाम भुगतना) = accept unpleasant consequences.</b><br>Example: “He had to face the music after the error was discovered.”<br>A concert is literal, and avoidance is the opposite.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Deal with consequences.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000072063","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"What is the synonym of the word “serene”? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Calm"},"2":{"en":"Bright"},"3":{"en":"Angry"},"4":{"en":"Disturbed"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Serene (शांत) = calm and peaceful.</b><br><b>Calm (शांत)</b> = peaceful ✔<br><b>Bright (चमकीला)</b> = shining<br><b>Angry (क्रोधित)</b> = irate; <b>disturbed (अशांत)</b> = agitated.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Calm.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000072064","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Phrasal Verbs","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>Unable to handle the sustained pressure, the junior associate eventually ___ during the audit. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"broke out"},"2":{"en":"broke away"},"3":{"en":"broke down"},"4":{"en":"broke off"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Break down (टूट जाना) = lose emotional or mental control.</b><br>Sustained pressure caused the associate to break down.<br><b>Break out</b> = escape or begin suddenly; <b>break away</b> = separate<br><b>Break off</b> = discontinue<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): broke down.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000072065","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>The ambassador's statement was meticulously phrased to maintain diplomatic decorum while subtly ___ criticism. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"deflecting"},"2":{"en":"inflicting"},"3":{"en":"reflecting"},"4":{"en":"injecting"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Inject (डालना) = introduce an element subtly.</b><br>The ambassador inserted criticism without violating diplomatic decorum.<br>“Deflecting” means turning criticism away.<br>“Inflicting” means imposing harm, and “reflecting” means showing.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): injecting.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000072066","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select “No substitution required”.<br>The journalist was more shocked than <b>any political reporter</b>. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"all political reporters"},"2":{"en":"other political reporters"},"3":{"en":"any of the political reporters"},"4":{"en":"No substitution required"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>The original comparative construction is acceptable.</b><br>“More shocked than any political reporter” compares the journalist with every reporter individually.<br>No exclusion word is needed if the journalist is not identified as a political reporter.<br>No substitution is required.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): other political reporters.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000072067","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. Visitors are required to register at the reception desk.<br>2. They are provided with temporary ID badges.<br>3. Security personnel verify their details.<br>4. Access to the premises is then granted. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-3-2-4"},"2":{"en":"3-1-2-4"},"3":{"en":"1-2-3-4"},"4":{"en":"2-1-3-4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-3-2-4</b><br>Visitors register, and security verifies their details.<br>Temporary ID badges are issued.<br>Access is granted last.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1-3-2-4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000072068","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In the 21st century, outer space has evolved from a scientific frontier into a geopolitical theatre where diplomacy, commerce, and national security intersect. The concept of space diplomacy—using cooperation and negotiation in outer space affairs as tools of statecraft—has become central to the foreign policy strategies of both emerging and established powers. It is no longer sufficient for nations to launch satellites; they must now navigate orbital politics. The strategic importance of space assets—from communication satellites to Earth observation systems—has redefined the contours of sovereignty and surveillance. Increasingly, countries are leveraging space-based capabilities for soft power projection, offering satellite data to developing nations, sharing launch infrastructure, and even co-developing space missions. Such cooperation enhances diplomatic goodwill while simultaneously extending geopolitical influence. India’s space diplomacy, for instance, has matured from technological self-reliance to regional leadership. The South Asia Satellite, launched by ISRO in 2017, was a watershed moment—offering communication and meteorological services to neighbouring countries as a “gift.” However, even as such projects are framed as acts of regional solidarity, they reinforce India's leadership narrative in the subcontinent. Yet, this domain is not without contest. The increasing militarization of space, signaled by the creation of dedicated space forces and the testing of anti-satellite weapons (ASATs), adds a layer of strategic mistrust. The absence of updated, binding international treaties governing weaponization and satellite security further complicates multilateral coordination. At the same time, the entry of private players into the space ecosystem introduces commercial diplomacy. Tech giants and start-ups now collaborate with governments in dual-use ventures—civilian technologies with potential military applications. As regulatory frameworks struggle to keep pace, diplomacy must adapt not only to intergovernmental negotiations but also to corporate interests. In essence, space diplomacy is about managing cooperation amid competition. As Low Earth Orbit becomes increasingly crowded and lunar exploration re-emerges as a theatre of contest, future diplomacy must balance ambition with restraint. Nations that excel in this balance will shape not just the future of outer space—but also the geopolitical alignments back on Earth.<br><br><br>According to the passage, why is space no longer a purely scientific domain? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It has become fully commercialized"},"2":{"en":"It involves geopolitical, strategic, and economic stakes"},"3":{"en":"Nations have stopped funding basic research"},"4":{"en":"Only private companies now operate in space"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Space now joins diplomacy, commerce and national security.</b><br>Orbital assets affect sovereignty, surveillance and geopolitical influence.<br>The passage does not claim full commercialization or an end to research.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): It involves geopolitical, strategic, and economic stakes.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000072069","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In the 21st century, outer space has evolved from a scientific frontier into a geopolitical theatre where diplomacy, commerce, and national security intersect. The concept of space diplomacy—using cooperation and negotiation in outer space affairs as tools of statecraft—has become central to the foreign policy strategies of both emerging and established powers. It is no longer sufficient for nations to launch satellites; they must now navigate orbital politics. The strategic importance of space assets—from communication satellites to Earth observation systems—has redefined the contours of sovereignty and surveillance. Increasingly, countries are leveraging space-based capabilities for soft power projection, offering satellite data to developing nations, sharing launch infrastructure, and even co-developing space missions. Such cooperation enhances diplomatic goodwill while simultaneously extending geopolitical influence. India’s space diplomacy, for instance, has matured from technological self-reliance to regional leadership. The South Asia Satellite, launched by ISRO in 2017, was a watershed moment—offering communication and meteorological services to neighbouring countries as a “gift.” However, even as such projects are framed as acts of regional solidarity, they reinforce India's leadership narrative in the subcontinent. Yet, this domain is not without contest. The increasing militarization of space, signaled by the creation of dedicated space forces and the testing of anti-satellite weapons (ASATs), adds a layer of strategic mistrust. The absence of updated, binding international treaties governing weaponization and satellite security further complicates multilateral coordination. At the same time, the entry of private players into the space ecosystem introduces commercial diplomacy. Tech giants and start-ups now collaborate with governments in dual-use ventures—civilian technologies with potential military applications. As regulatory frameworks struggle to keep pace, diplomacy must adapt not only to intergovernmental negotiations but also to corporate interests. In essence, space diplomacy is about managing cooperation amid competition. As Low Earth Orbit becomes increasingly crowded and lunar exploration re-emerges as a theatre of contest, future diplomacy must balance ambition with restraint. Nations that excel in this balance will shape not just the future of outer space—but also the geopolitical alignments back on Earth.<br><br><br>What does the passage imply about projects like India’s South Asia Satellite? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They are entirely altruistic and non-strategic"},"2":{"en":"They are technical exercises with no diplomatic implications"},"3":{"en":"They serve regional cooperation while advancing soft power"},"4":{"en":"They breach international norms"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: The satellite offers regional services while reinforcing India’s leadership.</b><br>Cooperation and strategic influence operate together.<br>It is not purely altruistic, merely technical or a treaty breach.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): They serve regional cooperation while advancing soft power.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000072070","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In the 21st century, outer space has evolved from a scientific frontier into a geopolitical theatre where diplomacy, commerce, and national security intersect. The concept of space diplomacy—using cooperation and negotiation in outer space affairs as tools of statecraft—has become central to the foreign policy strategies of both emerging and established powers. It is no longer sufficient for nations to launch satellites; they must now navigate orbital politics. The strategic importance of space assets—from communication satellites to Earth observation systems—has redefined the contours of sovereignty and surveillance. Increasingly, countries are leveraging space-based capabilities for soft power projection, offering satellite data to developing nations, sharing launch infrastructure, and even co-developing space missions. Such cooperation enhances diplomatic goodwill while simultaneously extending geopolitical influence. India’s space diplomacy, for instance, has matured from technological self-reliance to regional leadership. The South Asia Satellite, launched by ISRO in 2017, was a watershed moment—offering communication and meteorological services to neighbouring countries as a “gift.” However, even as such projects are framed as acts of regional solidarity, they reinforce India's leadership narrative in the subcontinent. Yet, this domain is not without contest. The increasing militarization of space, signaled by the creation of dedicated space forces and the testing of anti-satellite weapons (ASATs), adds a layer of strategic mistrust. The absence of updated, binding international treaties governing weaponization and satellite security further complicates multilateral coordination. At the same time, the entry of private players into the space ecosystem introduces commercial diplomacy. Tech giants and start-ups now collaborate with governments in dual-use ventures—civilian technologies with potential military applications. As regulatory frameworks struggle to keep pace, diplomacy must adapt not only to intergovernmental negotiations but also to corporate interests. In essence, space diplomacy is about managing cooperation amid competition. As Low Earth Orbit becomes increasingly crowded and lunar exploration re-emerges as a theatre of contest, future diplomacy must balance ambition with restraint. Nations that excel in this balance will shape not just the future of outer space—but also the geopolitical alignments back on Earth.<br><br><br>The entry of private players in space has introduced which new diplomatic challenge? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Decline in government-funded research"},"2":{"en":"Obsolescence of multilateral organizations"},"3":{"en":"Need to negotiate with non-state entities"},"4":{"en":"Violation of arms control treaties"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Diplomacy must adapt to corporate interests as well as governments.</b><br>Private companies create commercial and dual-use concerns requiring negotiation.<br>The passage does not declare research or multilateral bodies obsolete.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Need to negotiate with non-state entities.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000072071","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In the 21st century, outer space has evolved from a scientific frontier into a geopolitical theatre where diplomacy, commerce, and national security intersect. The concept of space diplomacy—using cooperation and negotiation in outer space affairs as tools of statecraft—has become central to the foreign policy strategies of both emerging and established powers. It is no longer sufficient for nations to launch satellites; they must now navigate orbital politics. The strategic importance of space assets—from communication satellites to Earth observation systems—has redefined the contours of sovereignty and surveillance. Increasingly, countries are leveraging space-based capabilities for soft power projection, offering satellite data to developing nations, sharing launch infrastructure, and even co-developing space missions. Such cooperation enhances diplomatic goodwill while simultaneously extending geopolitical influence. India’s space diplomacy, for instance, has matured from technological self-reliance to regional leadership. The South Asia Satellite, launched by ISRO in 2017, was a watershed moment—offering communication and meteorological services to neighbouring countries as a “gift.” However, even as such projects are framed as acts of regional solidarity, they reinforce India's leadership narrative in the subcontinent. Yet, this domain is not without contest. The increasing militarization of space, signaled by the creation of dedicated space forces and the testing of anti-satellite weapons (ASATs), adds a layer of strategic mistrust. The absence of updated, binding international treaties governing weaponization and satellite security further complicates multilateral coordination. At the same time, the entry of private players into the space ecosystem introduces commercial diplomacy. Tech giants and start-ups now collaborate with governments in dual-use ventures—civilian technologies with potential military applications. As regulatory frameworks struggle to keep pace, diplomacy must adapt not only to intergovernmental negotiations but also to corporate interests. In essence, space diplomacy is about managing cooperation amid competition. As Low Earth Orbit becomes increasingly crowded and lunar exploration re-emerges as a theatre of contest, future diplomacy must balance ambition with restraint. Nations that excel in this balance will shape not just the future of outer space—but also the geopolitical alignments back on Earth.<br><br><br>Why does the passage suggest that space diplomacy must balance ambition with restraint? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To maintain technological superiority"},"2":{"en":"Because LEO is becoming unsafe"},"3":{"en":"To avoid breaching the Outer Space Treaty"},"4":{"en":"To ensure sustainable cooperation amid strategic competition"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Space diplomacy manages cooperation amid competition.</b><br>Crowded orbits and renewed lunar rivalry make restraint essential.<br>The goal is sustainable cooperation, not superiority alone.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): To ensure sustainable cooperation amid strategic competition.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000072072","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage and answer the questions based on the passage:<br><br>In the 21st century, outer space has evolved from a scientific frontier into a geopolitical theatre where diplomacy, commerce, and national security intersect. The concept of space diplomacy—using cooperation and negotiation in outer space affairs as tools of statecraft—has become central to the foreign policy strategies of both emerging and established powers. It is no longer sufficient for nations to launch satellites; they must now navigate orbital politics. The strategic importance of space assets—from communication satellites to Earth observation systems—has redefined the contours of sovereignty and surveillance. Increasingly, countries are leveraging space-based capabilities for soft power projection, offering satellite data to developing nations, sharing launch infrastructure, and even co-developing space missions. Such cooperation enhances diplomatic goodwill while simultaneously extending geopolitical influence. India’s space diplomacy, for instance, has matured from technological self-reliance to regional leadership. The South Asia Satellite, launched by ISRO in 2017, was a watershed moment—offering communication and meteorological services to neighbouring countries as a “gift.” However, even as such projects are framed as acts of regional solidarity, they reinforce India's leadership narrative in the subcontinent. Yet, this domain is not without contest. The increasing militarization of space, signaled by the creation of dedicated space forces and the testing of anti-satellite weapons (ASATs), adds a layer of strategic mistrust. The absence of updated, binding international treaties governing weaponization and satellite security further complicates multilateral coordination. At the same time, the entry of private players into the space ecosystem introduces commercial diplomacy. Tech giants and start-ups now collaborate with governments in dual-use ventures—civilian technologies with potential military applications. As regulatory frameworks struggle to keep pace, diplomacy must adapt not only to intergovernmental negotiations but also to corporate interests. In essence, space diplomacy is about managing cooperation amid competition. As Low Earth Orbit becomes increasingly crowded and lunar exploration re-emerges as a theatre of contest, future diplomacy must balance ambition with restraint. Nations that excel in this balance will shape not just the future of outer space—but also the geopolitical alignments back on Earth.<br><br><br>Which of the following can be inferred from the passage? [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Space weaponization is regulated effectively"},"2":{"en":"Corporate players have no role in diplomacy"},"3":{"en":"Space diplomacy now includes non-traditional actors and dual-use dilemmas"},"4":{"en":"Nations avoid using space for strategic purposes"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Tech firms collaborate in civilian technologies with military applications.</b><br>These non-state actors complicate diplomacy and regulation.<br>Weaponization is not effectively regulated, and strategic uses are increasing.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Space diplomacy now includes non-traditional actors and dual-use dilemmas.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000072073","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:<br>The new constitutional provision is likely to be challenged by legal activists. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Legal activists have been likely to challenge the new constitutional provision."},"2":{"en":"Legal activists are likely to challenge the new constitutional provision."},"3":{"en":"Legal activists will be likely to challenge the new constitutional provision."},"4":{"en":"Legal activists were likely to challenge the new constitutional provision."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The passive agent becomes the active subject.</b><br>“Is likely to be challenged” becomes “are likely to challenge.”<br>The constitutional provision remains the object.<br>The other options alter tense or use incorrect aspect.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Legal activists are likely to challenge the new constitutional provision..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000072074","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>NEFARIOUS</b> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Just"},"2":{"en":"Virtuous"},"3":{"en":"Good"},"4":{"en":"wicked"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Nefarious (दुष्ट) = wicked or criminal.</b><br><b>Just (न्यायपूर्ण)</b> = fair<br><b>Virtuous (सदाचारी)</b> = moral<br><b>Good (अच्छा)</b> = virtuous<br><b>Wicked (दुष्ट)</b> = evil ✔<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): wicked.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000072075","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Detrimental</b> [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Helpful"},"2":{"en":"Harmful"},"3":{"en":"Damaging"},"4":{"en":"Toxic"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Detrimental (हानिकारक) = harmful.</b><br><b>Helpful (लाभदायक)</b> = beneficial ✔<br><b>Harmful (हानिकारक)</b> = damaging<br><b>Damaging (क्षतिकर)</b> = injurious; <b>toxic (विषैला)</b> = poisonous.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Helpful.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000072076","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a word meaning “beyond physical”. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Metaphysics"},"2":{"en":"Metaphisics"},"3":{"en":"Metaphesics"},"4":{"en":"Metaphyzics"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Metaphysics (तत्त्वमीमांसा) = philosophy beyond physical phenomena.</b><br>The correct spelling is “metaphysics.”<br><b>Metaphisics</b> replaces “y” with “i.”<br><b>Metaphesics</b> and <b>metaphyzics</b> alter the vowel or consonant.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Metaphysics.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000072077","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a Jurassic “first bird”. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Archeopteryx"},"2":{"en":"Archaeopterix"},"3":{"en":"Archaeopteryx"},"4":{"en":"Archaopteryx"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Archaeopteryx (आर्कियोप्टेरिक्स) = an extinct Jurassic bird-like dinosaur.</b><br>The correct spelling is “archaeopteryx.”<br><b>Archeopteryx</b> omits “a”; <b>archaeopterix</b> uses “i.”<br><b>Archaopteryx</b> omits “e.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Archaeopteryx.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000072078","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “A person who is skilled in beautiful handwriting”. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Numismatist"},"2":{"en":"Archivist"},"3":{"en":"Philatelist"},"4":{"en":"calligrapher"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Calligrapher (सुलेखक) = a person skilled in decorative handwriting.</b><br><b>Numismatist</b> = coin scholar<br><b>Archivist</b> = keeper of records<br><b>Philatelist</b> = stamp collector<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): calligrapher.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000072079","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the misspelt word. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Assiduous"},"2":{"en":"Lambent"},"3":{"en":"Malapropism"},"4":{"en":"Prestegious"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Prestigious (प्रतिष्ठित) = respected and admired.</b><br><b>Prestegious</b> incorrectly uses “e” instead of “i.”<br><b>Assiduous</b> = diligent; <b>lambent</b> = softly glowing.<br><b>Malapropism</b> = mistaken use of a word.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Prestegious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000072080","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>The <b>gaffe</b> cost the candidate valuable public support. [SSC CGL 28/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The sailors hoisted the gaffe to adjust the sail."},"2":{"en":"The ambassador apologized for the diplomatic gaffe."},"3":{"en":"His verbal gaffe went viral within hours."},"4":{"en":"The comedian's gaffe was interpreted as offensive."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Gaffe = a social mistake; gaff = a spar used on a sailing vessel.</b><br>The original means an embarrassing blunder.<br>Option A uses a nautical referent, treating “gaffe” as equipment.<br>The other options retain the blunder meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The sailors hoisted the gaffe to adjust the sail..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};